\n    71→   - Location: Character name normalization\n    72→\n    73→5. **Too many common words in pronunciation guide (65+ in \"Other\")**\n    74→   - Problem: Common words like \"dauntless\", \"chiming\", \"magnificence\", \"casements\" are flagged\n    75→   - Location: Pronunciation flagging threshold\n    76→\n    77→6. **Foreign word false positive: \"decorum\"**\n    78→   - Problem: \"decorum\" flagged as foreign word - it's standard English (Latin-derived but fully assimilated)\n    79→   - Location: Foreign word detection\n    80→\n    81→## Root Cause Analysis: Why 11 Attempts Have Failed\n    82→\n    83→### Summary of All Failed Attempts\n    84→\n    85→| Attempt | Fix Applied | Result |\n    86→|---------|-------------|--------|\n    87→| 1 | Cross-group epithet resolution | No effect |\n    88→| 2 | Proper name with article classification | Caused regression - merge started |\n    89→| 3 | Added CRITICAL RULE #5 about confrontation in prompt | No effect |\n    90→| 4 | Implemented `_entities_in_confrontation()` function | No effect |\n    91→| 5 | Solo pattern matching for confrontation | No effect |\n    92→| 6 | (Evaluation only, no new fix) | No effect |\n    93→| 7 | Increased context window 150/120 -> 400 chars | No effect |\n    94→| 8 | Hard-coded death relationship detection | No effect |\n    95→| 9 | Increased context windows to 600-800, added death rule #6 | No effect |\n    96→| 10 | Fixed death relationship detection (check ALL contexts) | No effect |\n    97→| 11 | Increased mention_context_chars 100 -> 200 | Minimal effect (+0.15 score) |\n    98→\n    99→### The Fundamental Problem\n   100→\n   101→After 11 attempts targeting:\n   102→- Cross-group resolution: 10 attempts, NO effect\n   103→- Context window (mention extraction): 1 attempt, MINIMAL effect\n   104→\n   105→**CONCLUSION: The merge is NOT happening where we've been looking.**\n   106→\n   107→### Critical Evidence\n   108→\n   109→The **chapter summary pipeline CORRECTLY identifies 2 characters:**\n   110→- \"Prince Prospero\"\n   111→- \"The masked figure (Red Death)\"\n   112→\n   113→**But the character extraction pipeline merges them into 1.**\n   114→\n   115→This proves:\n   116→1. The underlying text analysis CAN distinguish these characters\n   117→2. The merge decision is happening OUTSIDE of cross-group resolution\n   118→3. All 11 attempts have been fixing the WRONG code location\n   119→\n   120→### Where Is the Merge Actually Happening?\n   121→\n   122→We have eliminated:\n   123→- ✗ Cross-group resolution (10 attempts, no effect)\n   124→- ✗ Mention context window size (1 attempt, minimal effect)\n   125→\n   126→Remaining possibilities:\n   127→\n   128→1. **Initial NER entity grouping** - spaCy may be grouping \"mummer\" with \"Prospero\" at extraction time based on proximity/coreference\n   129→2. **Single-group resolution** - Before cross-group, entities within a single proposed group may be pre-merged\n   130→3. **Proposer-level consensus** - Multiple proposers may agree to merge before cross-group resolution runs\n   131→4. **Entity classification stage** - \"the mummer\" may be classified as an epithet for Prospero at entity classification time\n   132→5. **Character merging post-processor** - Final cleanup may re-merge characters\n   133→\n   134→### Recommended Next Approach\n   135→\n   136→**CRITICAL: STOP modifying cross-group resolution code - 11 attempts prove the bug is not there.**\n   137→\n   138→1. **Add comprehensive tracing** at the PROPOSER level:\n   139→   - What entities does each proposer extract for \"the mummer\"?\n   140→   - What group does each proposer assign \"the mummer\" to?\n   141→   - Is \"the mummer\" being associated with Prospero BEFORE consensus runs?\n   142→\n   143→2. **Examine the NER extraction stage** in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/`:\n   144→   - How does spaCy classify \"the mummer\"?\n   145→   - Is coreference resolution linking \"the mummer\" to \"Prospero\"?\n   146→\n   147→3. **Add a DEBUG environment variable** to dump intermediate state:\n   148→   - Proposer outputs before consensus\n   149→   - Consensus input (what pairs are being considered)\n   150→   - Cross-group resolution input (what groups exist)\n   151→\n   152→4. **Consider inverting the problem**:\n   153→   - Since the summary pipeline correctly identifies 2 characters, can we use the summary output to VALIDATE/CORRECT character extraction?\n   154→   - Add a post-processing step: \"If the chapter summary mentions character X as distinct from character Y, they should NOT be merged\"\n   155→\n   156→## Fix History\n   157→\n   158→### Attempt 11 Fixes Applied\n   159→1. **Increased mention context window** (src/agents/config.py line 72)\n   160→   - Changed `character_mention_context_chars` from 100 -> 200 characters\n   161→   - Rationale: Death scene spans 190 chars, needed wider context\n   162→   - Result: Score improved 6.70 -> 6.85 but merge still occurs\n   163→   - **Conclusion: Context window was NOT the bottleneck**\n   164→\n   165→### Attempts 1-10 Fixes\n   166→See git history for full details. All targeted cross-group resolution in `consensus.py` - none succeeded.\n   167→\n   168→## Output Files\n   169→- HTML: output/masque_of_red_death/report.html\n   170→- JSON: output/masque_of_red_death/analysis.json\n   171→\n   172→## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 11)\n   173→- Analysis completed in 7m 28s\n   174→- Total LLM tokens: 35,769\n   175→- Character count: 1 (STILL showing merge issue - \"the Prince Prospero (aka Prospero, the mummer)\")\n   176→- Pipeline bottleneck: Character Extraction (67.8% of time, 5m11s)\n   177→\n   178→## Key Observation\n   179→\n   180→**The chapter summary pipeline CORRECTLY identifies 2 characters:**\n   181→- \"Prince Prospero\"\n   182→- \"The masked figure (Red Death)\"\n   183→\n   184→**But the character extraction pipeline merges them into 1.**\n   185→\n   186→This proves the information IS available. 