ce Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black chamber, where the figure is found to be empty, revealing the Red Death has infiltrated even their sanctuary. The plague then claims every reveller, the clock stops, the lights die, and darkness and decay reign supreme.\"\n    34→    }\n    35→  ],\n    36→  \"characters\": [\n    37→    {\n    38→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    39→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    40→      \"aliases\": [\n    41→        \"Prospero\",\n    42→        \"the mummer\"\n    43→      ],\n    44→      \"role\": null,\n    45→      \"appearance\": null,\n    46→      \"personality\": null,\n    47→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    48→      \"descriptions\": [\n    49→        {\n    50→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a noble figure who retreats with a thousand courtiers into a sealed abbey to escape the Red Death, hosting a lavish masked ball during the height of the plague. He exhibits a shift from confidence and authority to rage and desperation when confronted by a masked figure resembling the Red Death, ultimately dying upon contact with the intruder in the black chamber.\",\n    51→          \"source_position\": 1894,\n    52→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    53→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    54→        }\n    55→      ],\n    56→      \"relationships\": {},\n    57→      \"evidence\": [\n    58→        {\n    59→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero retreats with a thousand courtiers into a sealed abbey to avoid the Red Death\",\n    60→          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero seals himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to avoid the plague\",\n    61→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n    62→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    63→        },\n    64→        {\n    65→          \"statement\": \"He hosts a lavish masked ball during the plague\",\n