NIST\\n    42→   - Evidence from text:\\n    43→     - \\\"seizing the mummer, whose tall figure stood erect and motionless within the shadow of the ebony clock\\\"\\n    44→     - \\\"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\\\" (Prospero DIES after confronting the mummer)\\n    45→     - The mummer is \\\"dressed as the Red Death itself, draped in grave-cloths\\\"\\n    46→     - When unmasked, the figure is \\\"untenanted by any tangible form\\\" (not a person at all)\\n    47→   - Impact: The main antagonist is merged with the protagonist (-2 point character score minimum)\\n    48→   - **ELEVEN attempts have now failed to fix this issue**\\n    49→   - Location: **STILL UNKNOWN** - not in cross-group resolution, context window increase did not help\\n    50→\\n    51→2. **Missing character: The Red Death / Masked Figure**\\n    52→   - Problem: The antagonist of the story should be its own character entry\\n    53→   - Aliases that should be grouped together:\\n    54→     - \\\"the figure\\\" / \\\"the masked figure\\\"\\n    55→     - \\\"the stranger\\\"\\n    56→     - \\\"the intruder\\\"\\n    57→     - \\\"the mummer\\\"\\n    58→     - \\\"the Red Death\\\" (personification)\\n    59→   - Evidence: Chapter summary CORRECTLY identifies two characters: \\\"Prince Prospero\\\" and \\\"The masked figure (Red Death)\\\" - but character extraction merges them\\n    60→   - Impact: Major character missing from analysis\\n    61→   - Note: Will emerge naturally once issue #1 is fixed\\n    62→\\n    63→### HIGH\\n    64→3. **Missing alias: \\\"the duke\\\" for Prince Prospero**\\n    65→   - Problem: Text uses \\\"the duke\\\" to refer to Prospero: \\\"as might have been expected from the duke's love of the bizarre\\\"\\n    66→   - Location: Alias detection\\n    67→\\n    68→### MEDIUM\\n    69→4. **Canonical name format includes leading article**\\n    70→   - Problem: Character name is \\\"the Prince Prospero\\\" instead of \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n    