e\\n   108→\\n   109→The **chapter summary pipeline CORRECTLY identifies 2 characters:**\\n   110→- \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n   111→- \\\"The masked figure (Red Death)\\\"\\n   112→\\n   113→**But the character extraction pipeline merges them into 1.**\\n   114→\\n   115→This proves:\\n   116→1. The underlying text analysis CAN distinguish these characters\\n   117→2. The merge decision is happening OUTSIDE of cross-group resolution\\n   118→3. All 11 attempts have been fixing the WRONG code location\\n   119→\\n   120→### Where Is the Merge Actually Happening?\\n   121→\\n   122→We have eliminated:\\n   123→- ✗ Cross-group resolution (10 attempts, no effect)\\n   124→- ✗ Mention context window size (1 attempt, minimal effect)\\n   125→\\n   126→Remaining possibilities:\\n   127→\\n   128→1. **Initial NER entity grouping** - spaCy may be grouping \\\"mummer\\\" with \\\"Prospero\\\" at extraction time based on proximity/coreference\\n   129→2. **Single-group resolution** - Before cross-group, entities within a single proposed group may be pre-merged\\n   130→3. **Proposer-level consensus** - Multiple proposers may agree to merge before cross-group resolution runs\\n   131→4. **Entity classification stage** - \\\"the mummer\\\" may be classified as an epithet for Prospero at entity classification time\\n   132→5. **Character merging post-processor** - Final cleanup may re-merge characters\\n   133→\\n   134→### Recommended Next Approach\\n   135→\\n   136→**CRITICAL: STOP modifying cross-group resolution code - 11 attempts prove the bug is not there.**\\n   137→\\n   138→1. **Add comprehensive tracing** at the PROPOSER level:\\n   139→   - What entities does each proposer extract for \\\"the mummer\\\"?\\n   140→   - What group does each proposer assign \\\"the mummer\\\" to?\\n   141→   - Is \\\"the mummer\\\" being associated with Prospero BEFORE consensus runs?\\n   142→\\n   143→2. **Examine the NER extraction stage** in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/`:\\n 