ontent\":\"Read root cause analysis and understand the merge issue\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Reading root cause analysis\"},{\"content\":\"Trace data flow: where does 'the mummer' get associated with Prince Prospero?\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Tracing data flow for character merge\"},{\"content\":\"Add diagnostic tracing at proposer level to identify merge location\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Adding diagnostic tracing\"},{\"content\":\"Implement fix based on root cause findings\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Implementing fix\"},{\"content\":\"Run smoke test on 2-3 chapters to verify fix\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Running smoke test\"},{\"content\":\"Update EVALUATION_STATE.md with fix details\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Updating evaluation state\"}]}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01FumZGPH5wtPJbSFMhcupbg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Based on my reading, the situation is critical:\\n\\n## Understanding the Problem\\n\\nAfter **11 failed attempts**, all targeting cross-group resolution and context windows, the fundamental issue persists: **\\\"the mummer\\\" (Red Death) is incorrectly merged with Prince Prospero**, despite them being distinct characters where one kills the other.\\n\\nThe key insight from EVALUATION_STATE.md is:\\n- The **chapter summary pipeline CORRECTLY identifies 2 characters**\\n- But **character extraction merges them into 1**\\n- All 11 attempts modified cross-group resolution code with **ZERO effect**\\n\\nThis proves the merge is happening **BEFORE** cross-group resolution runs.\\n\\n## Phase 1: ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS\\n\\nLet me trace the character extraction pipeline to find where the merge actually occurs:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":323,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36899,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":323,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"1801a8bb-6ebb-4d62-9ad1-ddd7e2f6a4d4\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01FumZGPH5wtPJbSFMhcupbg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01CcKrPmjc1ox7Zees4ma6kg\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/agents/characters.py\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":323,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36899,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":323,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"e4d90a9d-0c1b-490b-ac9d-0c21c0cd6ff5\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01FumZGPH5wtPJbSFMhcupbg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_013gRqc8jrQVFcqMk4553sjF\",\"name\":\"Glob\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"src/pipeline/character_extraction/**/*.py\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":323,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36899,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":323,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"a20717d4-6f39-47c2-a20b-78607990bb25\"}\n--\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01VxwGsovQS1Pb4UtwoPzLAY\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_013nqytephNKoi6AsQf5gZ1d\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/pipeline.py\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":6,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":9784,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":37222,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":9784,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"53ff7e4b-9332-45c0-b187-e1f98b96d338\"}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_013nqytephNKoi6AsQf5gZ1d\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     2→Character extraction pipeline orchestrator.\\n     3→\\n     4→Coordinates the full character extraction workflow with checkpointing.\\n     5→\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     6→\\n     7→import hashlib\\n     8→from pathlib import Path\\n     9→from datetime import datetime\\n    10→from typing import Optional, Callable\\n    11→import logging\\n    12→\\n    13→from .models import (\\n    14→    CharacterProposal,\\n    15→    CharacterValidationResult,\\n    16→    CharacterMap,\\n    17→    CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n    18→)\\n    19→from .proposers import BaseCharacterProposer, NERProposer, LLMCharacterProposer, create_coreference_proposer\\n    20→from .validator import CharacterValidator\\n    21→from .consensus import CharacterConsensusBuilder\\n    22→from ..chapter_detection.models import ChapterMap as ChapterDetectionMap\\n    23→from ..llm import LLMClient\\n    24→\\n    25→logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n    26→\\n    27→\\n    28→class CharacterExtractionPipeline:\\n    29→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    30→    Orchestrates the full character extraction workflow.\\n    31→\\n    32→    Stages:\\n    33→    1. Extraction: Run proposers on each chapter\\n    34→    2. Validation: Validate each proposal\\n    35→    3. Consensus: Merge across chapters, resolve aliases\\n    36→\\n    37→    Supports checkpointing to save/resume progress.\\n    38→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    39→\\n    40→    def __init__(\\n    41→        self,\\n    42→        llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\\n    43→        proposers: Optional[list[BaseCharacterProposer]] = None,\\n    44→        validator: Optional[CharacterValidator] = None,\\n    45→        consensus_builder: Optional[CharacterConsensusBuilder] = None,\\n    46→        checkpoint_dir: Optional[Path] = None,\\n    47→        progress_callback: Optional[Callable[[str, int, int], None]] = None,\\n    48→        llm_chunk_size: int = 8000,\\n    49→        mention_context_window: int = 100,\\n    50→        enable_coreference: bool = False,\\n    51→    ):\\n    52→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    53→        Args:\\n    54→            llm_client: LLM client for LLM-based extraction and validation\\n    55→            proposers: List of character proposers (default: NER + LLM if client provided)\\n    56→            validator: Character validator instance\\n    57→            consensus_builder: Consensus builder instance\\n    58→            checkpoint_dir: Directory for saving checkpoints\\n    59→            progress_callback: Callback(stage, current, total) for progress updates\\n    60→            enable_coreference: Whether to enable coreference resolution (requires coreferee)\\n    61→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    62→        self.llm = llm_client\\n    63→        self.checkpoint_dir = checkpoint_dir\\n    64→        self.progress_callback = progress_callback\\n    65→\\n    66→        # Set up proposers\\n    67→        if proposers is not None:\\n    68→            self.proposers = proposers\\n    69→        else:\\n    70→            self.proposers = [NERProposer(context_window=mention_context_window)]\\n    71→            if llm_client:\\n    72→                self.proposers.append(LLMCharacterProposer(\\n    73→                    llm_client,\\n    74→                    chunk_size=llm_chunk_size,\\n    75→                    context_window=mention_context_window,\\n    76→                ))\\n    77→            # Add coreference proposer if enabled and available\\n    78→            if enable_coreference:\\n    79→                coref_proposer = create_coreference_proposer(\\n    80→                    context_window=mention_context_window\\n    81→                )\\n    82→                if coref_proposer:\\n    83→                    self.proposers.append(coref_proposer)\\n    84→                    logger.info(\\\"Coreference proposer enabled\\\")\\n    85→\\n    86→        # Set up validator\\n    87→        self.validator = validator or CharacterValidator(\\n    88→            llm_client=llm_client,\\n    89→            use_llm_validation=llm_client is not None,\\n    90→        )\\n    91→\\n    92→        # Set up consensus builder\\n    93→        self.consensus_builder = consensus_builder or CharacterConsensusBuilder(\\n    94→            llm_client=llm_client,\\n    95→            use_llm_alias_resolution=llm_client is not None,\\n    96→        )\\n    97→\\n    98→    def run(\\n    99→        self,\\n   100→        full_text: str,\\n   101→        chapter_map: ChapterDetectionMap,\\n   102→        source_file: str = \\\"unknown\\\",\\n   103→        resume_from: Optional[CharacterPipelineCheckpoint] = None,\\n   104→    ) -> tuple[CharacterMap, CharacterPipelineCheckpoint]:\\n   105→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   106→        Run the full character extraction pipeline.\\n   107→\\n   108→        Args:\\n   109→            full_text: The complete document text\\n   110→            chapter_map: Chapter boundaries from chapter detection\\n   111→            source_file: Source file name for checkpointing\\n   112→            resume_from: Optional checkpoint to resume from\\n   113→\\n   114→        Returns:\\n   115→            Tuple of (CharacterMap, final checkpoint)\\n   116→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   117→        # Calculate text hash for checkpoint validation\\n   118→        text_hash = hashlib.md5(full_text.encode()).hexdigest()\\n   119→\\n   120→        # Initialize or validate checkpoint\\n   121→        if resume_from:\\n   122→            if resume_from.text_hash != text_hash:\\n   123→                logger.warning(\\\"Text hash mismatch - starting fresh\\\")\\n   124→                checkpoint = CharacterPipelineCheckpoint.create_new(source_file, text_hash)\\n   125→            else:\\n   126→                checkpoint = resume_from\\n   127→                logger.info(f\\\"Resuming from stage: {checkpoint.stage}\\\")\\n   128→        else:\\n   129→            checkpoint = CharacterPipelineCheckpoint.create_new(source_file, text_hash)\\n   130→\\n   131→        import time as _time  # Local import for timing\\n   132→\\n   133→        # Stage 1: Extraction\\n   134→        if checkpoint.stage == \\\"extraction\\\":\\n   135→            stage_start = _time.perf_counter()\\n   136→            logger.info(\\\"Stage 1: Character extraction from chapters\\\")\\n   137→            checkpoint = self._run_extraction(full_text, chapter_map, checkpoint)\\n   138→            self._save_checkpoint(checkpoint)\\n   139→            elapsed = _time.perf_counter() - stage_start\\n   140→            logger.info(f\\\"Stage 1 completed in {elapsed:.1f}s\\\")\\n   141→\\n   142→        # Stage 2: Validation\\n   143→        if checkpoint.stage == \\\"validation\\\":\\n   144→            stage_start = _time.perf_counter()\\n   145→            logger.info(\\\"Stage 2: Validating character proposals\\\")\\n   146→            checkpoint = self._run_validation(checkpoint)\\n   147→            self._save_checkpoint(checkpoint)\\n   148→            elapsed = _time.perf_counter() - stage_start\\n   149→            logger.info(f\\\"Stage 2 completed in {elapsed:.1f}s\\\")\\n   150→\\n   151→        # Stage 3: Consensus\\n   152→        if checkpoint.stage == \\\"consensus\\\":\\n   153→            stage_start = _time.perf_counter()\\n   154→            logger.info(\\\"Stage 3: Building cross-chapter consensus\\\")\\n   155→            checkpoint = self._run_consensus(checkpoint, len(chapter_map.chapters))\\n   156→            self._save_checkpoint(checkpoint)\\n   157→            elapsed = _time.perf_counter() - stage_start\\n   158→            logger.info(f\\\"Stage 3 completed in {elapsed:.1f}s\\\")\\n   159→\\n   160→        return checkpoint.character_map, checkpoint\\n   161→\\n   162→    def _run_extraction(\\n   163→        self,\\n   164→        full_text: str,\\n   165→        chapter_map: ChapterDetectionMap,\\n   166→        checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n   167→    ) -> CharacterPipelineCheckpoint:\\n   168→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Run character extraction on all chapters.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   169→        chapter_proposals = {}\\n   170→        total_chapters = len(chapter_map.chapters)\\n   171→\\n   172→        for i, chapter in enumerate(chapter_map.chapters):\\n   173→            chapter_idx = chapter.index\\n   174→            self._report_progress(\\\"extraction\\\", i + 1, total_chapters)\\n   175→\\n   176→            # Extract chapter text\\n   177→            start = chapter.start_position\\n   178→            end = chapter.end_position\\n   179→            chapter_text = full_text[start:end]\\n   180→\\n   181→            # Run all proposers\\n   182→            proposals = []\\n   183→            for proposer in self.proposers:\\n   184→                try:\\n   185→                    prop_results = proposer.propose(\\n   186→                        chapter_text=chapter_text,\\n   187→                        chapter_index=chapter_idx,\\n   188→                        chapter_start_position=start,\\n   189→                    )\\n   190→                    proposals.extend(prop_results)\\n   191→                    logger.debug(\\n   192→                        f\\\"  {proposer.name}: found {len(prop_results)} proposals \\\"\\n   193→                        f\\\"in chapter {chapter_idx}\\\"\\n   194→                    )\\n   195→                except Exception as e:\\n   196→                    logger.error(f\\\"Proposer {proposer.name} failed on chapter {chapter_idx}: {e}\\\")\\n   197→                    checkpoint.errors.append(\\n   198→                        f\\\"Proposer {proposer.name} failed on chapter {chapter_idx}: {str(e)}\\\"\\n   199→                    )\\n   200→                    # Re-raise to fail fast instead of continuing with errors\\n   201→                    raise\\n   202→\\n   203→            chapter_proposals[chapter_idx] = proposals\\n   204→            logger.info(\\n   205→                f\\\"Chapter {chapter_idx}: {len(proposals)} total proposals from \\\"\\n   206→                f\\\"{len(self.proposers)} proposers\\\"\\n   207→            )\\n   208→\\n   209→        checkpoint.chapter_proposals = chapter_proposals\\n   210→        checkpoint.stage = \\\"validation\\\"\\n   211→        checkpoint.timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat()\\n   212→\\n   213→        return checkpoint\\n   214→\\n   215→    def _run_validation(\\n   216→        self,\\n   217→        checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n   218→    ) -> CharacterPipelineCheckpoint:\\n   219→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Validate all character proposals.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   220→        if not checkpoint.chapter_proposals:\\n   221→            checkpoint.warnings.append(\\\"No chapter proposals to validate\\\")\\n   222→            checkpoint.validations = []\\n   223→            checkpoint.stage = \\\"consensus\\\"\\n   224→            return checkpoint\\n   225→\\n   226→        # Flatten all proposals\\n   227→        all_proposals = []\\n   228→        for chapter_idx, proposals in checkpoint.chapter_proposals.items():\\n   229→            all_proposals.extend(proposals)\\n   230→\\n   231→        # IMPORTANT:\\n   232→        # We cache validations by normalized name to avoid redundant LLM calls,\\n   233→        # but we still emit a validation result for EVERY proposal.\\n   234→        #\\n   235→        # Why: downstream consensus/alias resolution needs per-chapter distribution\\n   236→        # (mentions + chapter coverage). Deduplicating proposals before validation\\n   237→        # discards that evidence and can significantly hurt merge accuracy.\\n   238→        total_proposals = len(all_proposals)\\n   239→        unique_names = len({p.name.lower().strip() for p in all_proposals})\\n   240→        logger.info(\\n   241→            f\\\"Validating {total_proposals} proposals across {unique_names} unique names \\\"\\n   242→            f\\\"(caching enabled to avoid redundant LLM calls)\\\"\\n   243→        )\\n   244→\\n   245→        validation_cache: dict[str, CharacterValidationResult] = {}\\n   246→        validations: list[CharacterValidationResult] = []\\n   247→\\n   248→        for i, proposal in enumerate(all_proposals):\\n   249→            self._report_progress(\\\"validation\\\", i + 1, total_proposals)\\n   250→\\n   251→            norm_name = proposal.name.lower().strip()\\n   252→\\n   253→            # If we've already validated this NAME, reuse the decision but keep\\n   254→            # the original proposal (and its mentions/chapter index) for consensus.\\n   255→            if norm_name in validation_cache:\\n   256→                cached = validation_cache[norm_name]\\n   257→                validations.append(CharacterValidationResult(\\n   258→                    proposal=proposal,\\n   259→                    is_person_score=cached.is_person_score,\\n   260→                    context_score=cached.context_score,\\n   261→                    alias_candidates=list(cached.alias_candidates),\\n   262→                    overall_score=cached.overall_score,\\n   263→                    is_valid=cached.is_valid,\\n   264→                    reasoning=cached.reasoning,\\n   265→                ))\\n   266→                continue\\n   267→\\n   268→            try:\\n   269→                result = self.validator.validate(proposal)\\n   270→                validation_cache[norm_name] = result\\n   271→                validations.append(result)\\n   272→            except Exception as e:\\n   273→                logger.error(f\\\"Validation failed for '{proposal.name}': {e}\\\")\\n   274→                checkpoint.errors.append(f\\\"Validation failed for '{proposal.name}': {str(e)}\\\")\\n   275→                # Re-raise to fail fast instead of continuing with errors\\n   276→                raise\\n   277→\\n   278→        valid_count = sum(1 for v in validations if v.is_valid)\\n   279→        logger.info(f\\\"Validation complete: {valid_count}/{total_proposals} valid (cached {len(validation_cache)} unique names)\\\")\\n   280→\\n   281→        checkpoint.validations = validations\\n   282→        checkpoint.stage = \\\"consensus\\\"\\n   283→        checkpoint.timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat()\\n   284→\\n   285→        return checkpoint\\n   286→\\n   287→    def _run_consensus(\\n   288→        self,\\n   289→        checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n   290→        total_chapters: int,\\n   291→    ) -> CharacterPipelineCheckpoint:\\n   292→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Build consensus across all chapters.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   293→        if not checkpoint.validations:\\n   294→            checkpoint.character_map = CharacterMap(\\n   295→                characters=[],\\n   296→                low_confidence_characters=[],\\n   297→                total_mentions=0,\\n   298→                total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n   299→                pipeline_metadata={\\\"warning\\\": \\\"No validations to build consensus from\\\"},\\n   300→            )\\n   301→            checkpoint.stage = \\\"complete\\\"\\n   302→            return checkpoint\\n   303→\\n   304→        self._report_progress(\\\"consensus\\\", 1, 1)\\n   305→\\n   306→        try:\\n   307→            character_map = self.consensus_builder.build_consensus(\\n   308→                validations=checkpoint.validations,\\n   309→                total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n   310→            )\\n   311→            checkpoint.character_map = character_map\\n   312→            logger.info(\\n   313→                f\\\"Consensus complete: {len(character_map.characters)} characters, \\\"\\n   314→                f\\\"{len(character_map.low_confidence_characters)} low-confidence\\\"\\n   315→            )\\n   316→        except Exception as e:\\n   317→            logger.error(f\\\"Consensus building failed: {e}\\\")\\n   318→            checkpoint.errors.append(f\\\"Consensus building failed: {str(e)}\\\")\\n   319→            # Re-raise to fail fast instead of returning empty character map\\n   320→            raise\\n   321→\\n   322→        checkpoint.stage = \\\"complete\\\"\\n   323→        checkpoint.timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat()\\n   324→\\n   325→        return checkpoint\\n   326→\\n   327→    def _save_checkpoint(self, checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint) -> None:\\n   328→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Save checkpoint to disk if checkpoint_dir is configured.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   329→        if not self.checkpoint_dir:\\n   330→            return\\n   331→\\n   332→        self.checkpoint_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n   333→\\n   334→        # Use source file name for checkpoint file\\n   335→        safe_name = Path(checkpoint.source_file).stem\\n   336→        checkpoint_file = self.checkpoint_dir / f\\\"characters_{safe_name}.json\\\"\\n   337→\\n   338→        try:\\n   339→            checkpoint.save(checkpoint_file)\\n   340→            logger.debug(f\\\"Checkpoint saved: {checkpoint_file}\\\")\\n   341→        except Exception as e:\\n   342→            logger.error(f\\\"Failed to save checkpoint: {e}\\\")\\n   343→\\n   344→    def _report_progress(self, stage: str, current: int, total: int) -> None:\\n   345→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Report progress if callback is configured.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   346→        if self.progress_callback:\\n   347→            self.progress_callback(stage, current, total)\\n   348→\\n   349→\\n   350→def extract_characters(\\n   351→    full_text: str,\\n   352→    chapter_map: ChapterDetectionMap,\\n   353→    llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\\n   354→    checkpoint_dir: Optional[Path] = None,\\n   355→    source_file: str = \\\"unknown\\\",\\n   356→    progress_callback: Optional[Callable[[str, int, int], None]] = None,\\n   357→) -> CharacterMap:\\n   358→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   359→    Convenience function for character extraction.\\n   360→\\n   361→    Args:\\n   362→        full_text: Complete document text\\n   363→        chapter_map: Chapter boundaries from chapter detection\\n   364→        llm_client: Optional LLM client\\n   365→        checkpoint_dir: Optional directory for checkpoints\\n   366→        source_file: Source file name\\n   367→        progress_callback: Optional progress callback\\n   368→\\n   369→    Returns:\\n   370→        CharacterMap with extracted characters\\n   371→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   372→    pipeline = CharacterExtractionPipeline(\\n   373→        llm_client=llm_client,\\n   374→        checkpoint_dir=checkpoint_dir,\\n   375→        progress_callback=progress_callback,\\n   376→    )\\n   377→\\n   378→    character_map, _ = pipeline.run(\\n   379→        full_text=full_text,\\n   380→        chapter_map=chapter_map,\\n   381→        source_file=source_file,\\n   382→    )\\n   383→\\n   384→    return character_map\\n   385→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"9455e8aa-577a-4be4-9bad-5bfee2df2cc6\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/pipeline.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nCharacter extraction pipeline orchestrator.\\n\\nCoordinates the full character extraction workflow with checkpointing.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport hashlib\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\nfrom typing import Optional, Callable\\nimport logging\\n\\nfrom .models import (\\n    CharacterProposal,\\n    CharacterValidationResult,\\n    CharacterMap,\\n    CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n)\\nfrom .proposers import BaseCharacterProposer, NERProposer, LLMCharacterProposer, create_coreference_proposer\\nfrom .validator import CharacterValidator\\nfrom .consensus import CharacterConsensusBuilder\\nfrom ..chapter_detection.models import ChapterMap as ChapterDetectionMap\\nfrom ..llm import LLMClient\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n\\n\\nclass CharacterExtractionPipeline:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Orchestrates the full character extraction workflow.\\n\\n    Stages:\\n    1. Extraction: Run proposers on each chapter\\n    2. Validation: Validate each proposal\\n    3. Consensus: Merge across chapters, resolve aliases\\n\\n    Supports checkpointing to save/resume progress.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(\\n        self,\\n        llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\\n        proposers: Optional[list[BaseCharacterProposer]] = None,\\n        validator: Optional[CharacterValidator] = None,\\n        consensus_builder: Optional[CharacterConsensusBuilder] = None,\\n        checkpoint_dir: Optional[Path] = None,\\n        progress_callback: Optional[Callable[[str, int, int], None]] = None,\\n        llm_chunk_size: int = 8000,\\n        mention_context_window: int = 100,\\n        enable_coreference: bool = False,\\n    ):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Args:\\n            llm_client: LLM client for LLM-based extraction and validation\\n            proposers: List of character proposers (default: NER + LLM if client provided)\\n            validator: Character validator instance\\n            consensus_builder: Consensus builder instance\\n            checkpoint_dir: Directory for saving checkpoints\\n            progress_callback: Callback(stage, current, total) for progress updates\\n            enable_coreference: Whether to enable coreference resolution (requires coreferee)\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.llm = llm_client\\n        self.checkpoint_dir = checkpoint_dir\\n        self.progress_callback = progress_callback\\n\\n        # Set up proposers\\n        if proposers is not None:\\n            self.proposers = proposers\\n        else:\\n            self.proposers = [NERProposer(context_window=mention_context_window)]\\n            if llm_client:\\n                self.proposers.append(LLMCharacterProposer(\\n                    llm_client,\\n                    chunk_size=llm_chunk_size,\\n                    context_window=mention_context_window,\\n                ))\\n            # Add coreference proposer if enabled and available\\n            if enable_coreference:\\n                coref_proposer = create_coreference_proposer(\\n                    context_window=mention_context_window\\n                )\\n                if coref_proposer:\\n                    self.proposers.append(coref_proposer)\\n                    logger.info(\\\"Coreference proposer enabled\\\")\\n\\n        # Set up validator\\n        self.validator = validator or CharacterValidator(\\n            llm_client=llm_client,\\n            use_llm_validation=llm_client is not None,\\n        )\\n\\n        # Set up consensus builder\\n        self.consensus_builder = consensus_builder or CharacterConsensusBuilder(\\n            llm_client=llm_client,\\n            use_llm_alias_resolution=llm_client is not None,\\n        )\\n\\n    def run(\\n        self,\\n        full_text: str,\\n        chapter_map: ChapterDetectionMap,\\n        source_file: str = \\\"unknown\\\",\\n        resume_from: Optional[CharacterPipelineCheckpoint] = None,\\n    ) -> tuple[CharacterMap, CharacterPipelineCheckpoint]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Run the full character extraction pipeline.\\n\\n        Args:\\n            full_text: The complete document text\\n            chapter_map: Chapter boundaries from chapter detection\\n            source_file: Source file name for checkpointing\\n            resume_from: Optional checkpoint to resume from\\n\\n        Returns:\\n            Tuple of (CharacterMap, final checkpoint)\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # Calculate text hash for checkpoint validation\\n        text_hash = hashlib.md5(full_text.encode()).hexdigest()\\n\\n        # Initialize or validate checkpoint\\n        if resume_from:\\n            if resume_from.text_hash != text_hash:\\n                logger.warning(\\\"Text hash mismatch - starting fresh\\\")\\n                checkpoint = CharacterPipelineCheckpoint.create_new(source_file, text_hash)\\n            else:\\n                checkpoint = resume_from\\n                logger.info(f\\\"Resuming from stage: {checkpoint.stage}\\\")\\n        else:\\n            checkpoint = CharacterPipelineCheckpoint.create_new(source_file, text_hash)\\n\\n        import time as _time  # Local import for timing\\n\\n        # Stage 1: Extraction\\n        if checkpoint.stage == \\\"extraction\\\":\\n            stage_start = _time.perf_counter()\\n            logger.info(\\\"Stage 1: Character extraction from chapters\\\")\\n            checkpoint = self._run_extraction(full_text, chapter_map, checkpoint)\\n            self._save_checkpoint(checkpoint)\\n            elapsed = _time.perf_counter() - stage_start\\n            logger.info(f\\\"Stage 1 completed in {elapsed:.1f}s\\\")\\n\\n        # Stage 2: Validation\\n        if checkpoint.stage == \\\"validation\\\":\\n            stage_start = _time.perf_counter()\\n            logger.info(\\\"Stage 2: Validating character proposals\\\")\\n            checkpoint = self._run_validation(checkpoint)\\n            self._save_checkpoint(checkpoint)\\n            elapsed = _time.perf_counter() - stage_start\\n            logger.info(f\\\"Stage 2 completed in {elapsed:.1f}s\\\")\\n\\n        # Stage 3: Consensus\\n        if checkpoint.stage == \\\"consensus\\\":\\n            stage_start = _time.perf_counter()\\n            logger.info(\\\"Stage 3: Building cross-chapter consensus\\\")\\n            checkpoint = self._run_consensus(checkpoint, len(chapter_map.chapters))\\n            self._save_checkpoint(checkpoint)\\n            elapsed = _time.perf_counter() - stage_start\\n            logger.info(f\\\"Stage 3 completed in {elapsed:.1f}s\\\")\\n\\n        return checkpoint.character_map, checkpoint\\n\\n    def _run_extraction(\\n        self,\\n        full_text: str,\\n        chapter_map: ChapterDetectionMap,\\n        checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n    ) -> CharacterPipelineCheckpoint:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Run character extraction on all chapters.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        chapter_proposals = {}\\n        total_chapters = len(chapter_map.chapters)\\n\\n        for i, chapter in enumerate(chapter_map.chapters):\\n            chapter_idx = chapter.index\\n            self._report_progress(\\\"extraction\\\", i + 1, total_chapters)\\n\\n            # Extract chapter text\\n            start = chapter.start_position\\n            end = chapter.end_position\\n            chapter_text = full_text[start:end]\\n\\n            # Run all proposers\\n            proposals = []\\n            for proposer in self.proposers:\\n                try:\\n                    prop_results = proposer.propose(\\n                        chapter_text=chapter_text,\\n                        chapter_index=chapter_idx,\\n                        chapter_start_position=start,\\n                    )\\n                    proposals.extend(prop_results)\\n                    logger.debug(\\n                        f\\\"  {proposer.name}: found {len(prop_results)} proposals \\\"\\n                        f\\\"in chapter {chapter_idx}\\\"\\n                    )\\n                except Exception as e:\\n                    logger.error(f\\\"Proposer {proposer.name} failed on chapter {chapter_idx}: {e}\\\")\\n                    checkpoint.errors.append(\\n                        f\\\"Proposer {proposer.name} failed on chapter {chapter_idx}: {str(e)}\\\"\\n                    )\\n                    # Re-raise to fail fast instead of continuing with errors\\n                    raise\\n\\n            chapter_proposals[chapter_idx] = proposals\\n            logger.info(\\n                f\\\"Chapter {chapter_idx}: {len(proposals)} total proposals from \\\"\\n                f\\\"{len(self.proposers)} proposers\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n        checkpoint.chapter_proposals = chapter_proposals\\n        checkpoint.stage = \\\"validation\\\"\\n        checkpoint.timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat()\\n\\n        return checkpoint\\n\\n    def _run_validation(\\n        self,\\n        checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n    ) -> CharacterPipelineCheckpoint:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Validate all character proposals.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not checkpoint.chapter_proposals:\\n            checkpoint.warnings.append(\\\"No chapter proposals to validate\\\")\\n            checkpoint.validations = []\\n            checkpoint.stage = \\\"consensus\\\"\\n            return checkpoint\\n\\n        # Flatten all proposals\\n        all_proposals = []\\n        for chapter_idx, proposals in checkpoint.chapter_proposals.items():\\n            all_proposals.extend(proposals)\\n\\n        # IMPORTANT:\\n        # We cache validations by normalized name to avoid redundant LLM calls,\\n        # but we still emit a validation result for EVERY proposal.\\n        #\\n        # Why: downstream consensus/alias resolution needs per-chapter distribution\\n        # (mentions + chapter coverage). Deduplicating proposals before validation\\n        # discards that evidence and can significantly hurt merge accuracy.\\n        total_proposals = len(all_proposals)\\n        unique_names = len({p.name.lower().strip() for p in all_proposals})\\n        logger.info(\\n            f\\\"Validating {total_proposals} proposals across {unique_names} unique names \\\"\\n            f\\\"(caching enabled to avoid redundant LLM calls)\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n        validation_cache: dict[str, CharacterValidationResult] = {}\\n        validations: list[CharacterValidationResult] = []\\n\\n        for i, proposal in enumerate(all_proposals):\\n            self._report_progress(\\\"validation\\\", i + 1, total_proposals)\\n\\n            norm_name = proposal.name.lower().strip()\\n\\n            # If we've already validated this NAME, reuse the decision but keep\\n            # the original proposal (and its mentions/chapter index) for consensus.\\n            if norm_name in validation_cache:\\n                cached = validation_cache[norm_name]\\n                validations.append(CharacterValidationResult(\\n                    proposal=proposal,\\n                    is_person_score=cached.is_person_score,\\n                    context_score=cached.context_score,\\n                    alias_candidates=list(cached.alias_candidates),\\n                    overall_score=cached.overall_score,\\n                    is_valid=cached.is_valid,\\n                    reasoning=cached.reasoning,\\n                ))\\n                continue\\n\\n            try:\\n                result = self.validator.validate(proposal)\\n                validation_cache[norm_name] = result\\n                validations.append(result)\\n            except Exception as e:\\n                logger.error(f\\\"Validation failed for '{proposal.name}': {e}\\\")\\n                checkpoint.errors.append(f\\\"Validation failed for '{proposal.name}': {str(e)}\\\")\\n                # Re-raise to fail fast instead of continuing with errors\\n                raise\\n\\n        valid_count = sum(1 for v in validations if v.is_valid)\\n        logger.info(f\\\"Validation complete: {valid_count}/{total_proposals} valid (cached {len(validation_cache)} unique names)\\\")\\n\\n        checkpoint.validations = validations\\n        checkpoint.stage = \\\"consensus\\\"\\n        checkpoint.timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat()\\n\\n        return checkpoint\\n\\n    def _run_consensus(\\n        self,\\n        checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint,\\n        total_chapters: int,\\n    ) -> CharacterPipelineCheckpoint:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Build consensus across all chapters.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not checkpoint.validations:\\n            checkpoint.character_map = CharacterMap(\\n                characters=[],\\n                low_confidence_characters=[],\\n                total_mentions=0,\\n                total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n                pipeline_metadata={\\\"warning\\\": \\\"No validations to build consensus from\\\"},\\n            )\\n            checkpoint.stage = \\\"complete\\\"\\n            return checkpoint\\n\\n        self._report_progress(\\\"consensus\\\", 1, 1)\\n\\n        try:\\n            character_map = self.consensus_builder.build_consensus(\\n                validations=checkpoint.validations,\\n                total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n            )\\n            checkpoint.character_map = character_map\\n            logger.info(\\n                f\\\"Consensus complete: {len(character_map.characters)} characters, \\\"\\n                f\\\"{len(character_map.low_confidence_characters)} low-confidence\\\"\\n            )\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            logger.error(f\\\"Consensus building failed: {e}\\\")\\n            checkpoint.errors.append(f\\\"Consensus building failed: {str(e)}\\\")\\n            # Re-raise to fail fast instead of returning empty character map\\n            raise\\n\\n        checkpoint.stage = \\\"complete\\\"\\n        checkpoint.timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat()\\n\\n        return checkpoint\\n\\n    def _save_checkpoint(self, checkpoint: CharacterPipelineCheckpoint) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Save checkpoint to disk if checkpoint_dir is configured.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not self.checkpoint_dir:\\n            return\\n\\n        self.checkpoint_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n\\n        # Use source file name for checkpoint file\\n        safe_name = Path(checkpoint.source_file).stem\\n        checkpoint_file = self.checkpoint_dir / f\\\"characters_{safe_name}.json\\\"\\n\\n        try:\\n            checkpoint.save(checkpoint_file)\\n            logger.debug(f\\\"Checkpoint saved: {checkpoint_file}\\\")\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            logger.error(f\\\"Failed to save checkpoint: {e}\\\")\\n\\n    def _report_progress(self, stage: str, current: int, total: int) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Report progress if callback is configured.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self.progress_callback:\\n            self.progress_callback(stage, current, total)\\n\\n\\ndef extract_characters(\\n    full_text: str,\\n    chapter_map: ChapterDetectionMap,\\n    llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\\n    checkpoint_dir: Optional[Path] = None,\\n    source_file: str = \\\"unknown\\\",\\n    progress_callback: Optional[Callable[[str, int, int], None]] = None,\\n) -> CharacterMap:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Convenience function for character extraction.\\n\\n    Args:\\n        full_text: Complete document text\\n        chapter_map: Chapter boundaries from chapter detection\\n        llm_client: Optional LLM client\\n        checkpoint_dir: Optional directory for checkpoints\\n        source_file: Source file name\\n        progress_callback: Optional progress callback\\n\\n    Returns:\\n        CharacterMap with extracted characters\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    pipeline = CharacterExtractionPipeline(\\n        llm_client=llm_client,\\n        checkpoint_dir=checkpoint_dir,\\n        progress_callback=progress_callback,\\n    )\\n\\n    character_map, _ = pipeline.run(\\n        full_text=full_text,\\n        chapter_map=chapter_map,\\n        source_file=source_file,\\n    )\\n\\n    return character_map\\n\",\"numLines\":385,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":385}}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01W5yn8YVdecgtiUpNb5Ss4F\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now let me look at the consensus builder, which is where the cross-group resolution happens (that all 11 attempts have been modifying):\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5069,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":47006,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":5069,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"fd73251c-b3fd-4cf0-bdae-7211682eb71f\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01W5yn8YVdecgtiUpNb5Ss4F\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01AA6CrwcQJNgW2aaEPBopqw\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py\",\"limit\":300}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5069,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":47006,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":5069,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"33a63897-3df1-4345-aa9a-561a84d311c9\"}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01AA6CrwcQJNgW2aaEPBopqw\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     2→Cross-chapter character consensus builder.\\n     3→\\n     4→Merges character proposals across chapters, resolves aliases,\\n     5→and produces the final CharacterMap.\\n     6→\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     7→\\n     8→import re\\n     9→import hashlib\\n    10→import time\\n    11→from typing import Optional, Iterable\\n    12→from collections import defaultdict\\n    13→from difflib import SequenceMatcher\\n    14→import logging\\n    15→\\n    16→from .models import (\\n    17→    CharacterProposal,\\n    18→    CharacterValidationResult,\\n    19→    Character,\\n    20→    CharacterMap,\\n    21→    CharacterMention,\\n    22→    CharacterType,\\n    23→)\\n    24→from .constants import are_potential_nicknames, get_nickname_variants\\n    25→from ..llm import LLMClient\\n    26→\\n    27→logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n    28→\\n    29→# Character classification prompts\\n    30→CHARACTER_TYPE_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst classifying character types.\\n    31→\\n    32→Classify each character as one of:\\n    33→- STORY: An active participant in the narrative who appears in scenes, speaks dialogue, or takes actions\\n    34→- HISTORICAL: A real historical figure mentioned in passing (e.g., Napoleon, Einstein)\\n    35→- REFERENCED: A fictional character from other works mentioned in passing (e.g., Hamlet, Sherlock Holmes)\\n    36→\\n    37→Return ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    38→\\n    39→CHARACTER_TYPE_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Classify this character's role in the narrative.\\n    40→\\n    41→CHARACTER: {name}\\n    42→MENTION COUNT: {mention_count}\\n    43→CHAPTERS PRESENT: {chapters}\\n    44→SAMPLE CONTEXTS:\\n    45→{contexts}\\n    46→\\n    47→Based on the contexts, determine if this character:\\n    48→1. Actively participates (speaks, acts, appears in scenes) → STORY\\n    49→2. Is a real historical figure mentioned in passing → HISTORICAL\\n    50→3. Is a fictional character from other works → REFERENCED\\n    51→\\n    52→Return JSON:\\n    53→{{\\n    54→  \\\"character_type\\\": \\\"story\\\" | \\\"historical\\\" | \\\"referenced\\\",\\n    55→  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.0-1.0,\\n    56→  \\\"reason\\\": \\\"brief justification\\\"\\n    57→}}\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    58→\\n    59→# Common titles that should be ignored when comparing character names\\n    60→# These are not part of the actual name but indicate social status or role\\n    61→TITLES = {'mr', 'mrs', 'ms', 'miss', 'dr', 'sir', 'lady', 'lord', 'professor', 'captain', 'major'}\\n    62→\\n    63→# Epithet alias resolution prompt\\n    64→EPITHET_ALIAS_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying whether different descriptive handles (epithets) refer to the SAME unnamed character.\\n    65→\\n    66→Descriptive handles are phrases like \\\"the creature\\\", \\\"the monster\\\", \\\"the old man\\\", \\\"the detective\\\".\\n    67→\\n    68→CRITICAL RULES:\\n    69→1. Only merge epithets that CLEARLY refer to the same entity with HIGH CONFIDENCE\\n    70→2. Use chapter appearances and context clues to verify they're the same character\\n    71→3. Different descriptive characters (e.g., \\\"the old man\\\" in cottage vs \\\"the old man\\\" at inn) should NOT be merged\\n    72→4. Generic phrases that could refer to anyone should NOT be merged together\\n    73→\\n    74→Return ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    75→\\n    76→EPITHET_ALIAS_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Identify which descriptive handles refer to the SAME unnamed character.\\n    77→\\n    78→DESCRIPTIVE HANDLES (with chapter info and sample contexts):\\n    79→{epithets}\\n    80→\\n    81→For each group of handles that refer to the SAME entity:\\n    82→1. Pick the most specific/unique handle as canonical (e.g., \\\"the creature\\\" over \\\"the monster\\\")\\n    83→2. List all other handles as aliases\\n    84→\\n    85→Return JSON array:\\n    86→```json\\n    87→[\\n    88→  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"the creature\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": [\\\"the monster\\\", \\\"the wretch\\\", \\\"the fiend\\\"]}},\\n    89→  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"the old man\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": []}}\\n    90→]\\n    91→```\\n    92→\\n    93→Return ONLY the JSON array. Include only handles you're confident about - omit uncertain ones.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    94→\\n    95→# Cross-group (epithet-to-proper-name) resolution prompt\\n    96→CROSS_GROUP_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying whether descriptive handles (epithets) refer to named characters.\\n    97→\\n    98→Examples:\\n    99→- \\\"the prince\\\" might refer to \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n   100→- \\\"the duke\\\" might refer to \\\"Prince Prospero\\\" (if the story mentions he's also a duke)\\n   101→- \\\"the creature\\\" might refer to \\\"Adam\\\" (if named)\\n   102→- \\\"my father\\\" might refer to \\\"Alphonse Frankenstein\\\"\\n   103→\\n   104→CRITICAL RULES:\\n   105→1. Only link when context CLEARLY indicates they're the same person\\n   106→2. Use chapter co-appearances and context clues\\n   107→3. Titles/roles (the king, the general, my father) can refer to properly-named characters\\n   108→4. Generic epithets that could be anyone should NOT be linked\\n   109→5. DO NOT link if the epithet and proper name are in CONFLICT, OPPOSITION, or CONFRONTATION\\n   110→   - If context shows them interacting as separate entities, they are different people\\n   111→   - Examples: \\\"the intruder\\\" confronting \\\"Prince Prospero\\\", \\\"the stranger\\\" fighting \\\"the hero\\\"\\n   112→6. DO NOT link if one entity DIES in interaction with the other entity\\n   113→   - If context shows one character dying near/after encountering the other, they are DIFFERENT people\\n   114→   - Examples: \\\"fell prostrate in death\\\" near another entity, \\\"killed by\\\" another entity\\n   115→   - Death in proximity to another character means they cannot be the same person\\n   116→\\n   117→Return ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   118→\\n   119→CROSS_GROUP_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Identify which descriptive handles refer to properly-named characters.\\n   120→\\n   121→DESCRIPTIVE HANDLES:\\n   122→{epithets}\\n   123→\\n   124→NAMED CHARACTERS:\\n   125→{proper_names}\\n   126→\\n   127→IMPORTANT: Read the context snippets carefully. If an epithet and proper name appear in contexts showing them as SEPARATE ENTITIES (confronting, fighting, observing each other), DO NOT link them.\\n   128→\\n   129→For each epithet that CLEARLY refers to a named character, return a match.\\n   130→\\n   131→Return JSON array:\\n   132→```json\\n   133→[\\n   134→  {{\\\"epithet\\\": \\\"the prince\\\", \\\"proper_name\\\": \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"}},\\n   135→  {{\\\"epithet\\\": \\\"my father\\\", \\\"proper_name\\\": \\\"Alphonse Frankenstein\\\"}}\\n   136→]\\n   137→```\\n   138→\\n   139→Return ONLY the JSON array. Include only matches you're confident about - omit uncertain ones.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   140→\\n   141→PAIRWISE_ALIAS_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying whether two character names refer to the SAME PERSON.\\n   142→\\n   143→CRITICAL:\\n   144→- Use ONLY the evidence provided below (chapter appearances and context snippets).\\n   145→- Be conservative: false negatives (missing an alias) are better than false positives (merging different people).\\n   146→- Titles (Mr/Mrs/Miss/Dr/etc.) are not part of the name; treat them as address forms.\\n   147→\\n   148→Return ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   149→\\n   150→PAIRWISE_ALIAS_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Decide whether these two names refer to the SAME PERSON in this novel.\\n   151→\\n   152→NAME A: {name_a}\\n   153→MENTIONS A: {mentions_a}\\n   154→CHAPTERS A: {chapters_a}\\n   155→CONTEXT A:\\n   156→{contexts_a}\\n   157→\\n   158→NAME B: {name_b}\\n   159→MENTIONS B: {mentions_b}\\n   160→CHAPTERS B: {chapters_b}\\n   161→CONTEXT B:\\n   162→{contexts_b}\\n   163→\\n   164→Rules:\\n   165→- Only say same_person=true if there is strong evidence they are the same character (name overlap, title variants, obvious nickname/full-name relationship, or clear contextual cues).\\n   166→- If the only overlap is a last name, be VERY cautious (family members/spouses share last names).\\n   167→- If they never appear in overlapping chapters, be cautious unless it's clearly a full-name/short-name relationship.\\n   168→\\n   169→Return JSON:\\n   170→{{\\n   171→  \\\"same_person\\\": true/false,\\n   172→  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.0-1.0,\\n   173→  \\\"canonical\\\": \\\"Which of the two names should be canonical if same_person=true (must be exactly one of the provided names)\\\",\\n   174→  \\\"alias\\\": \\\"The other name if same_person=true (must be exactly one of the provided names)\\\",\\n   175→  \\\"reason\\\": \\\"brief justification\\\"\\n   176→}}\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   177→\\n   178→\\n   179→ALIAS_RESOLUTION_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying character aliases.\\n   180→\\n   181→Your task is to determine which character names refer to the SAME PERSON.\\n   182→\\n   183→IMPORTANT: Titles, ranks, and honorifics should be IGNORED when matching names.\\n   184→The underlying PERSON is what matters, not how they're addressed. Examples:\\n   185→- Military: \\\"SSgt Otto\\\" = \\\"Staff Sergeant Mark Otto\\\" = \\\"Mark Otto\\\" (but NOT just \\\"Otto\\\" alone)\\n   186→- Civilian: \\\"Mr. Smith\\\" = \\\"John Smith\\\" (but NOT just \\\"Smith\\\" alone - could be family member)\\n   187→- Religious: \\\"Father O'Brien\\\" = \\\"Patrick O'Brien\\\" (but NOT just \\\"O'Brien\\\" alone)\\n   188→- Academic: \\\"Professor Williams\\\" = \\\"Dr. Williams\\\" = \\\"Jane Williams\\\"\\n   189→\\n   190→CRITICAL RULES - BE CONSERVATIVE:\\n   191→1. Only merge names if they CLEARLY refer to the same individual with HIGH CONFIDENCE\\n   192→2. Different people with similar names should NEVER be merged\\n   193→3. Pay close attention to chapter appearances and context clues\\n   194→4. When in doubt, keep names SEPARATE - false negatives are better than false positives\\n   195→5. A bare FIRST name can merge with a full name (e.g., \\\"Mike\\\" → \\\"Michael Anderson\\\")\\n   196→6. A bare LAST name is RISKY - only merge if you're absolutely certain (could be family member)\\n   197→\\n   198→For the canonical name, prefer the FULL CIVILIAN NAME (first + last) over titled versions.\\n   199→\\n   200→NEVER merge:\\n   201→- Different characters who happen to share only a first name (e.g., two characters named Michael)\\n   202→- Different characters who share ONLY a last name (family members, spouses, siblings)\\n   203→  - \\\"Mr. Anderson\\\" (father) ≠ \\\"Michael\\\" (son) even if both are Andersons\\n   204→  - \\\"Robert Wilson\\\" ≠ \\\"Mrs. Wilson\\\" (his wife Emma)\\n   205→- Characters who appear in completely different parts of the book with no overlap\\n   206→- Names that are clearly different major characters (check mention counts - if both have 50+ mentions, they're probably separate people!)\\n   207→\\n   208→BE EXTREMELY CAUTIOUS WITH:\\n   209→- Bare last names (could be family members)\\n   210→- Gendered titles (Mr. vs Mrs. vs Miss suggests different people)\\n   211→- Characters with similar but different names (e.g., \\\"Michael\\\" vs \\\"Michelle\\\")\\n   212→\\n   213→SPECIFIC ANTI-PATTERNS (DO NOT MERGE):\\n   214→- Different first names + same last name (likely family members): spouses, siblings, parents/children\\n   215→- Single-word names with no overlap: completely different characters with unrelated names\\n   216→- Characters who co-occur but have different identities: appearing together ≠ being the same person\\n   217→\\n   218→ONLY merge when confident:\\n   219→1. Full name + partial name: full name contains the partial name as a component\\n   220→2. Title variations: titled form and untitled form of the same name\\n   221→3. Obvious nickname patterns: common nickname/full name pairs\\n   222→\\n   223→CRITICAL MERGE PATTERNS:\\n   224→\\n   225→MERGE these patterns (HIGH CONFIDENCE):\\n   226→- Full name variations: \\\"FirstName LastName\\\" = \\\"LastName\\\" = \\\"Title LastName\\\"\\n   227→- Nickname patterns: Shortened forms or diminutives of the same character\\n   228→- Birth/married names: Known alternate names for the same person (when contextually clear)\\n   229→\\n   230→DO NOT MERGE these patterns:\\n   231→- Title-only matches: Characters sharing only a title but different last names are DIFFERENT people\\n   232→- Family members: Different first names + same last name typically indicates spouses, siblings, or family (separate characters)\\n   233→- Similar titles: Same professional title (Professor, Doctor, Captain) doesn't indicate same person\\n   234→\\n   235→CONTEXTUAL CLUES to consider:\\n   236→- Relationship descriptors: \\\"his/her spouse\\\", \\\"his/her parent\\\", \\\"his/her sibling\\\" indicate SEPARATE characters\\n   237→- Gendered pronouns: Consistent he/she usage helps distinguish characters with ambiguous names\\n   238→- First-person narrative: First-person \\\"I\\\" may indicate narrator (check for self-references)\\n   239→\\n   240→MENTION COUNT HEURISTIC:\\n   241→- Large disparity (e.g., 200+ vs <10 mentions) often indicates full name vs shortened form\\n   242→- Similar counts (both >20 mentions) often indicates distinct characters of comparable importance\\n   243→\\n   244→When in doubt, keep SEPARATE. False negatives (missing an alias) are better than false positives (merging different characters).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   245→\\n   246→\\n   247→ALIAS_RESOLUTION_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Identify which character names refer to the SAME PERSON in this novel.\\n   248→\\n   249→CHARACTER NAMES (with chapter info and sample contexts):\\n   250→{characters}\\n   251→\\n   252→ANALYZE CAREFULLY:\\n   253→1. Check if names appear in similar chapters (overlapping chapters = might be same person)\\n   254→2. Check if contexts suggest the same person\\n   255→3. Look at mention counts - if both names have many mentions (50+), they're likely different major characters\\n   256→4. Check for gendered title conflicts (Mr. vs Mrs. suggests different people)\\n   257→5. When uncertain, keep names SEPARATE - it's better to have duplicates than to merge different people\\n   258→\\n   259→EXAMPLES OF CORRECT MERGES:\\n   260→- \\\"Sarah Miller\\\" + \\\"Sarah\\\" → SAME (first name matches full name)\\n   261→- \\\"Robert Chen\\\" + \\\"Chen\\\" + \\\"Mr. Chen\\\" → SAME (last name and titled version)\\n   262→- \\\"Michael Anderson\\\" + \\\"Mike\\\" → SAME (nickname matches full name)\\n   263→- \\\"Emma Wilson\\\" + \\\"Wilson\\\" + \\\"Miss Wilson\\\" → SAME (last name and titled version)\\n   264→- \\\"Dr. Williams\\\" + \\\"James Williams\\\" → SAME (titled version of full name)\\n   265→- \\\"Elizabeth Harper\\\" + \\\"Liz\\\" → SAME (nickname matches full name)\\n   266→\\n   267→EXAMPLES OF INCORRECT MERGES (DO NOT DO THIS!):\\n   268→- \\\"Mr. Anderson\\\" + \\\"Chen\\\" → WRONG! (completely different people, no name overlap)\\n   269→- \\\"Mr. Anderson\\\" + \\\"Emma\\\" → WRONG! (completely different people)\\n   270→- \\\"Mr. Roberts\\\" + \\\"Mrs. Roberts\\\" → WRONG! (likely spouses, different people)\\n   271→- \\\"Michael Brown\\\" + \\\"Sarah Brown\\\" → WRONG! (different people with same last name)\\n   272→- \\\"Sarah\\\" + \\\"Emma\\\" → WRONG! (different first names = different people)\\n   273→\\n   274→Return JSON array:\\n   275→```json\\n   276→[\\n   277→  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"Full Name\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": [\\\"Nickname\\\", \\\"Title LastName\\\"]}},\\n   278→  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"Another Character\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": []}}\\n   279→]\\n   280→```\\n   281→\\n   282→Return ONLY the JSON array. Include only names you're confident about - omit uncertain names entirely rather than making bad merges.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   283→\\n   284→\\n   285→class CharacterConsensusBuilder:\\n   286→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   287→    Builds consensus across chapters and resolves aliases.\\n   288→\\n   289→    Takes validated proposals from all chapters and produces\\n   290→    the final character map with merged mentions and aliases.\\n   291→    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   292→\\n   293→    def __init__(\\n   294→        self,\\n   295→        llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\\n   296→        confidence_threshold: float = 0.6,\\n   297→        use_llm_alias_resolution: bool = True,\\n   298→    ):\\n   299→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   300→        Args:\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"9563d51a-c520-464c-b4b9-ae6a195454fe\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nCross-chapter character consensus builder.\\n\\nMerges character proposals across chapters, resolves aliases,\\nand produces the final CharacterMap.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport re\\nimport hashlib\\nimport time\\nfrom typing import Optional, Iterable\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nfrom difflib import SequenceMatcher\\nimport logging\\n\\nfrom .models import (\\n    CharacterProposal,\\n    CharacterValidationResult,\\n    Character,\\n    CharacterMap,\\n    CharacterMention,\\n    CharacterType,\\n)\\nfrom .constants import are_potential_nicknames, get_nickname_variants\\nfrom ..llm import LLMClient\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n\\n# Character classification prompts\\nCHARACTER_TYPE_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst classifying character types.\\n\\nClassify each character as one of:\\n- STORY: An active participant in the narrative who appears in scenes, speaks dialogue, or takes actions\\n- HISTORICAL: A real historical figure mentioned in passing (e.g., Napoleon, Einstein)\\n- REFERENCED: A fictional character from other works mentioned in passing (e.g., Hamlet, Sherlock Holmes)\\n\\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nCHARACTER_TYPE_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Classify this character's role in the narrative.\\n\\nCHARACTER: {name}\\nMENTION COUNT: {mention_count}\\nCHAPTERS PRESENT: {chapters}\\nSAMPLE CONTEXTS:\\n{contexts}\\n\\nBased on the contexts, determine if this character:\\n1. Actively participates (speaks, acts, appears in scenes) → STORY\\n2. Is a real historical figure mentioned in passing → HISTORICAL\\n3. Is a fictional character from other works → REFERENCED\\n\\nReturn JSON:\\n{{\\n  \\\"character_type\\\": \\\"story\\\" | \\\"historical\\\" | \\\"referenced\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.0-1.0,\\n  \\\"reason\\\": \\\"brief justification\\\"\\n}}\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n# Common titles that should be ignored when comparing character names\\n# These are not part of the actual name but indicate social status or role\\nTITLES = {'mr', 'mrs', 'ms', 'miss', 'dr', 'sir', 'lady', 'lord', 'professor', 'captain', 'major'}\\n\\n# Epithet alias resolution prompt\\nEPITHET_ALIAS_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying whether different descriptive handles (epithets) refer to the SAME unnamed character.\\n\\nDescriptive handles are phrases like \\\"the creature\\\", \\\"the monster\\\", \\\"the old man\\\", \\\"the detective\\\".\\n\\nCRITICAL RULES:\\n1. Only merge epithets that CLEARLY refer to the same entity with HIGH CONFIDENCE\\n2. Use chapter appearances and context clues to verify they're the same character\\n3. Different descriptive characters (e.g., \\\"the old man\\\" in cottage vs \\\"the old man\\\" at inn) should NOT be merged\\n4. Generic phrases that could refer to anyone should NOT be merged together\\n\\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nEPITHET_ALIAS_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Identify which descriptive handles refer to the SAME unnamed character.\\n\\nDESCRIPTIVE HANDLES (with chapter info and sample contexts):\\n{epithets}\\n\\nFor each group of handles that refer to the SAME entity:\\n1. Pick the most specific/unique handle as canonical (e.g., \\\"the creature\\\" over \\\"the monster\\\")\\n2. List all other handles as aliases\\n\\nReturn JSON array:\\n```json\\n[\\n  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"the creature\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": [\\\"the monster\\\", \\\"the wretch\\\", \\\"the fiend\\\"]}},\\n  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"the old man\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": []}}\\n]\\n```\\n\\nReturn ONLY the JSON array. Include only handles you're confident about - omit uncertain ones.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n# Cross-group (epithet-to-proper-name) resolution prompt\\nCROSS_GROUP_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying whether descriptive handles (epithets) refer to named characters.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- \\\"the prince\\\" might refer to \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n- \\\"the duke\\\" might refer to \\\"Prince Prospero\\\" (if the story mentions he's also a duke)\\n- \\\"the creature\\\" might refer to \\\"Adam\\\" (if named)\\n- \\\"my father\\\" might refer to \\\"Alphonse Frankenstein\\\"\\n\\nCRITICAL RULES:\\n1. Only link when context CLEARLY indicates they're the same person\\n2. Use chapter co-appearances and context clues\\n3. Titles/roles (the king, the general, my father) can refer to properly-named characters\\n4. Generic epithets that could be anyone should NOT be linked\\n5. DO NOT link if the epithet and proper name are in CONFLICT, OPPOSITION, or CONFRONTATION\\n   - If context shows them interacting as separate entities, they are different people\\n   - Examples: \\\"the intruder\\\" confronting \\\"Prince Prospero\\\", \\\"the stranger\\\" fighting \\\"the hero\\\"\\n6. DO NOT link if one entity DIES in interaction with the other entity\\n   - If context shows one character dying near/after encountering the other, they are DIFFERENT people\\n   - Examples: \\\"fell prostrate in death\\\" near another entity, \\\"killed by\\\" another entity\\n   - Death in proximity to another character means they cannot be the same person\\n\\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nCROSS_GROUP_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Identify which descriptive handles refer to properly-named characters.\\n\\nDESCRIPTIVE HANDLES:\\n{epithets}\\n\\nNAMED CHARACTERS:\\n{proper_names}\\n\\nIMPORTANT: Read the context snippets carefully. If an epithet and proper name appear in contexts showing them as SEPARATE ENTITIES (confronting, fighting, observing each other), DO NOT link them.\\n\\nFor each epithet that CLEARLY refers to a named character, return a match.\\n\\nReturn JSON array:\\n```json\\n[\\n  {{\\\"epithet\\\": \\\"the prince\\\", \\\"proper_name\\\": \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"}},\\n  {{\\\"epithet\\\": \\\"my father\\\", \\\"proper_name\\\": \\\"Alphonse Frankenstein\\\"}}\\n]\\n```\\n\\nReturn ONLY the JSON array. Include only matches you're confident about - omit uncertain ones.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPAIRWISE_ALIAS_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying whether two character names refer to the SAME PERSON.\\n\\nCRITICAL:\\n- Use ONLY the evidence provided below (chapter appearances and context snippets).\\n- Be conservative: false negatives (missing an alias) are better than false positives (merging different people).\\n- Titles (Mr/Mrs/Miss/Dr/etc.) are not part of the name; treat them as address forms.\\n\\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No other text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPAIRWISE_ALIAS_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Decide whether these two names refer to the SAME PERSON in this novel.\\n\\nNAME A: {name_a}\\nMENTIONS A: {mentions_a}\\nCHAPTERS A: {chapters_a}\\nCONTEXT A:\\n{contexts_a}\\n\\nNAME B: {name_b}\\nMENTIONS B: {mentions_b}\\nCHAPTERS B: {chapters_b}\\nCONTEXT B:\\n{contexts_b}\\n\\nRules:\\n- Only say same_person=true if there is strong evidence they are the same character (name overlap, title variants, obvious nickname/full-name relationship, or clear contextual cues).\\n- If the only overlap is a last name, be VERY cautious (family members/spouses share last names).\\n- If they never appear in overlapping chapters, be cautious unless it's clearly a full-name/short-name relationship.\\n\\nReturn JSON:\\n{{\\n  \\\"same_person\\\": true/false,\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.0-1.0,\\n  \\\"canonical\\\": \\\"Which of the two names should be canonical if same_person=true (must be exactly one of the provided names)\\\",\\n  \\\"alias\\\": \\\"The other name if same_person=true (must be exactly one of the provided names)\\\",\\n  \\\"reason\\\": \\\"brief justification\\\"\\n}}\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nALIAS_RESOLUTION_SYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a literary analyst identifying character aliases.\\n\\nYour task is to determine which character names refer to the SAME PERSON.\\n\\nIMPORTANT: Titles, ranks, and honorifics should be IGNORED when matching names.\\nThe underlying PERSON is what matters, not how they're addressed. Examples:\\n- Military: \\\"SSgt Otto\\\" = \\\"Staff Sergeant Mark Otto\\\" = \\\"Mark Otto\\\" (but NOT just \\\"Otto\\\" alone)\\n- Civilian: \\\"Mr. Smith\\\" = \\\"John Smith\\\" (but NOT just \\\"Smith\\\" alone - could be family member)\\n- Religious: \\\"Father O'Brien\\\" = \\\"Patrick O'Brien\\\" (but NOT just \\\"O'Brien\\\" alone)\\n- Academic: \\\"Professor Williams\\\" = \\\"Dr. Williams\\\" = \\\"Jane Williams\\\"\\n\\nCRITICAL RULES - BE CONSERVATIVE:\\n1. Only merge names if they CLEARLY refer to the same individual with HIGH CONFIDENCE\\n2. Different people with similar names should NEVER be merged\\n3. Pay close attention to chapter appearances and context clues\\n4. When in doubt, keep names SEPARATE - false negatives are better than false positives\\n5. A bare FIRST name can merge with a full name (e.g., \\\"Mike\\\" → \\\"Michael Anderson\\\")\\n6. A bare LAST name is RISKY - only merge if you're absolutely certain (could be family member)\\n\\nFor the canonical name, prefer the FULL CIVILIAN NAME (first + last) over titled versions.\\n\\nNEVER merge:\\n- Different characters who happen to share only a first name (e.g., two characters named Michael)\\n- Different characters who share ONLY a last name (family members, spouses, siblings)\\n  - \\\"Mr. Anderson\\\" (father) ≠ \\\"Michael\\\" (son) even if both are Andersons\\n  - \\\"Robert Wilson\\\" ≠ \\\"Mrs. Wilson\\\" (his wife Emma)\\n- Characters who appear in completely different parts of the book with no overlap\\n- Names that are clearly different major characters (check mention counts - if both have 50+ mentions, they're probably separate people!)\\n\\nBE EXTREMELY CAUTIOUS WITH:\\n- Bare last names (could be family members)\\n- Gendered titles (Mr. vs Mrs. vs Miss suggests different people)\\n- Characters with similar but different names (e.g., \\\"Michael\\\" vs \\\"Michelle\\\")\\n\\nSPECIFIC ANTI-PATTERNS (DO NOT MERGE):\\n- Different first names + same last name (likely family members): spouses, siblings, parents/children\\n- Single-word names with no overlap: completely different characters with unrelated names\\n- Characters who co-occur but have different identities: appearing together ≠ being the same person\\n\\nONLY merge when confident:\\n1. Full name + partial name: full name contains the partial name as a component\\n2. Title variations: titled form and untitled form of the same name\\n3. Obvious nickname patterns: common nickname/full name pairs\\n\\nCRITICAL MERGE PATTERNS:\\n\\nMERGE these patterns (HIGH CONFIDENCE):\\n- Full name variations: \\\"FirstName LastName\\\" = \\\"LastName\\\" = \\\"Title LastName\\\"\\n- Nickname patterns: Shortened forms or diminutives of the same character\\n- Birth/married names: Known alternate names for the same person (when contextually clear)\\n\\nDO NOT MERGE these patterns:\\n- Title-only matches: Characters sharing only a title but different last names are DIFFERENT people\\n- Family members: Different first names + same last name typically indicates spouses, siblings, or family (separate characters)\\n- Similar titles: Same professional title (Professor, Doctor, Captain) doesn't indicate same person\\n\\nCONTEXTUAL CLUES to consider:\\n- Relationship descriptors: \\\"his/her spouse\\\", \\\"his/her parent\\\", \\\"his/her sibling\\\" indicate SEPARATE characters\\n- Gendered pronouns: Consistent he/she usage helps distinguish characters with ambiguous names\\n- First-person narrative: First-person \\\"I\\\" may indicate narrator (check for self-references)\\n\\nMENTION COUNT HEURISTIC:\\n- Large disparity (e.g., 200+ vs <10 mentions) often indicates full name vs shortened form\\n- Similar counts (both >20 mentions) often indicates distinct characters of comparable importance\\n\\nWhen in doubt, keep SEPARATE. False negatives (missing an alias) are better than false positives (merging different characters).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nALIAS_RESOLUTION_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"Identify which character names refer to the SAME PERSON in this novel.\\n\\nCHARACTER NAMES (with chapter info and sample contexts):\\n{characters}\\n\\nANALYZE CAREFULLY:\\n1. Check if names appear in similar chapters (overlapping chapters = might be same person)\\n2. Check if contexts suggest the same person\\n3. Look at mention counts - if both names have many mentions (50+), they're likely different major characters\\n4. Check for gendered title conflicts (Mr. vs Mrs. suggests different people)\\n5. When uncertain, keep names SEPARATE - it's better to have duplicates than to merge different people\\n\\nEXAMPLES OF CORRECT MERGES:\\n- \\\"Sarah Miller\\\" + \\\"Sarah\\\" → SAME (first name matches full name)\\n- \\\"Robert Chen\\\" + \\\"Chen\\\" + \\\"Mr. Chen\\\" → SAME (last name and titled version)\\n- \\\"Michael Anderson\\\" + \\\"Mike\\\" → SAME (nickname matches full name)\\n- \\\"Emma Wilson\\\" + \\\"Wilson\\\" + \\\"Miss Wilson\\\" → SAME (last name and titled version)\\n- \\\"Dr. Williams\\\" + \\\"James Williams\\\" → SAME (titled version of full name)\\n- \\\"Elizabeth Harper\\\" + \\\"Liz\\\" → SAME (nickname matches full name)\\n\\nEXAMPLES OF INCORRECT MERGES (DO NOT DO THIS!):\\n- \\\"Mr. Anderson\\\" + \\\"Chen\\\" → WRONG! (completely different people, no name overlap)\\n- \\\"Mr. Anderson\\\" + \\\"Emma\\\" → WRONG! (completely different people)\\n- \\\"Mr. Roberts\\\" + \\\"Mrs. Roberts\\\" → WRONG! (likely spouses, different people)\\n- \\\"Michael Brown\\\" + \\\"Sarah Brown\\\" → WRONG! (different people with same last name)\\n- \\\"Sarah\\\" + \\\"Emma\\\" → WRONG! (different first names = different people)\\n\\nReturn JSON array:\\n```json\\n[\\n  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"Full Name\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": [\\\"Nickname\\\", \\\"Title LastName\\\"]}},\\n  {{\\\"canonical\\\": \\\"Another Character\\\", \\\"aliases\\\": []}}\\n]\\n```\\n\\nReturn ONLY the JSON array. Include only names you're confident about - omit uncertain names entirely rather than making bad merges.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass CharacterConsensusBuilder:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Builds consensus across chapters and resolves aliases.\\n\\n    Takes validated proposals from all chapters and produces\\n    the final character map with merged mentions and aliases.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(\\n        self,\\n        llm_client: Optional[LLMClient] = None,\\n        confidence_threshold: float = 0.6,\\n        use_llm_alias_resolution: bool = True,\\n    ):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Args:\",\"numLines\":300,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":2317}}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01LMy79bhH2AnDY4XCxxPPpr\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me continue reading the consensus.py file to see how the build_consensus method works:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4598,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":52075,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":4598,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"44bf7062-88f9-463e-9e66-d428b7690bb9\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01LMy79bhH2AnDY4XCxxPPpr\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01AgmiKrpiR4cQJP4oU2Fx3Q\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py\",\"offset\":300,\"limit\":300}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4598,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":52075,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":4598,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"c5fe5f27-3000-46c2-9645-21b6a310b27b\"}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01AgmiKrpiR4cQJP4oU2Fx3Q\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"   300→        Args:\\n   301→            llm_client: LLM for alias resolution\\n   302→            confidence_threshold: Threshold for high-confidence characters\\n   303→            use_llm_alias_resolution: Whether to use LLM for alias resolution\\n   304→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   305→        self.llm = llm_client\\n   306→        self.confidence_threshold = confidence_threshold\\n   307→        self.use_llm_alias_resolution = use_llm_alias_resolution and llm_client is not None\\n   308→\\n   309→    def build_consensus(\\n   310→        self,\\n   311→        validations: list[CharacterValidationResult],\\n   312→        total_chapters: int,\\n   313→    ) -> CharacterMap:\\n   314→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   315→        Build the final character map from validated proposals.\\n   316→\\n   317→        Args:\\n   318→            validations: All validation results from all chapters\\n   319→            total_chapters: Total number of chapters in document\\n   320→\\n   321→        Returns:\\n   322→            Final CharacterMap with merged characters\\n   323→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   324→        logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: received {len(validations)} validations\\\")\\n   325→\\n   326→        # Filter to valid proposals\\n   327→        valid_results = [v for v in validations if v.is_valid]\\n   328→        invalid_count = len(validations) - len(valid_results)\\n   329→        if invalid_count > 0:\\n   330→            logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: filtered {invalid_count} invalid proposals\\\")\\n   331→\\n   332→        if not valid_results:\\n   333→            return CharacterMap(\\n   334→                characters=[],\\n   335→                low_confidence_characters=[],\\n   336→                total_mentions=0,\\n   337→                total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n   338→                pipeline_metadata={\\\"warning\\\": \\\"No valid character proposals found\\\"},\\n   339→            )\\n   340→\\n   341→        # Group by name (exact match first)\\n   342→        name_groups = self._group_by_name(valid_results)\\n   343→        logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: grouped into {len(name_groups)} unique names\\\")\\n   344→\\n   345→        # Log the top names by mention count\\n   346→        sorted_names = sorted(\\n   347→            name_groups.items(),\\n   348→            key=lambda x: sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in x[1]),\\n   349→            reverse=True\\n   350→        )\\n   351→        for name, results in sorted_names[:20]:\\n   352→            mentions = sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in results)\\n   353→            chapters = sorted(set(r.proposal.chapter_index for r in results))\\n   354→            logger.debug(f\\\"  '{name}': {mentions} mentions, chapters {chapters}\\\")\\n   355→        if len(sorted_names) > 20:\\n   356→            logger.debug(f\\\"  ... and {len(sorted_names) - 20} more names\\\")\\n   357→\\n   358→        # Separate proper names from descriptive handles\\n   359→        proper_name_groups = {}\\n   360→        epithet_groups = {}\\n   361→        for name, results in name_groups.items():\\n   362→            if self._is_descriptive_handle(name):\\n   363→                epithet_groups[name] = results\\n   364→                logger.debug(f\\\"Classified as epithet: '{name}'\\\")\\n   365→            else:\\n   366→                proper_name_groups[name] = results\\n   367→                logger.debug(f\\\"Classified as proper name: '{name}'\\\")\\n   368→\\n   369→        if epithet_groups:\\n   370→            logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: found {len(epithet_groups)} descriptive handles\\\")\\n   371→            logger.info(f\\\"Epithets: {list(epithet_groups.keys())}\\\")\\n   372→        if proper_name_groups:\\n   373→            logger.info(f\\\"Proper names: {list(proper_name_groups.keys())}\\\")\\n   374→\\n   375→        # Resolve aliases for proper names\\n   376→        if self.use_llm_alias_resolution and len(proper_name_groups) > 1:\\n   377→            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: using LLM alias resolution\\\")\\n   378→            alias_groups = self._llm_alias_resolution(proper_name_groups)\\n   379→        else:\\n   380→            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: using heuristic alias resolution\\\")\\n   381→            alias_groups = self._heuristic_alias_resolution(proper_name_groups, valid_results)\\n   382→\\n   383→        # Resolve aliases for epithets separately\\n   384→        if epithet_groups and self.use_llm_alias_resolution:\\n   385→            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: running epithet alias resolution\\\")\\n   386→            epithet_alias_groups = self._llm_epithet_resolution(epithet_groups)\\n   387→            # Merge epithet alias groups into main alias groups\\n   388→            for canonical, aliases in epithet_alias_groups.items():\\n   389→                alias_groups[canonical] = aliases\\n   390→        elif epithet_groups:\\n   391→            # No LLM - just add epithets as separate characters\\n   392→            for name in epithet_groups:\\n   393→                alias_groups[name] = []\\n   394→\\n   395→        # Cross-group resolution: link epithets to proper names (e.g., \\\"the prince\\\" -> \\\"Prince Prospero\\\")\\n   396→        if epithet_groups and proper_name_groups and self.use_llm_alias_resolution:\\n   397→            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: running cross-group (epithet-to-proper) resolution\\\")\\n   398→            cross_merges = self._llm_cross_group_resolution(epithet_groups, proper_name_groups)\\n   399→            # Apply cross-group merges\\n   400→            for epithet_name, proper_name in cross_merges.items():\\n   401→                if proper_name in alias_groups and epithet_name in alias_groups:\\n   402→                    # Add epithet as alias to proper name\\n   403→                    alias_groups[proper_name].append(epithet_name)\\n   404→                    # Also add any aliases the epithet had\\n   405→                    alias_groups[proper_name].extend(alias_groups[epithet_name])\\n   406→                    # Remove epithet as standalone character\\n   407→                    del alias_groups[epithet_name]\\n   408→                    logger.info(f\\\"Cross-group merge: '{proper_name}' <- epithet '{epithet_name}'\\\")\\n   409→\\n   410→        # Merge name_groups to include epithets for downstream processing\\n   411→        name_groups.update(epithet_groups)\\n   412→\\n   413→        # Log alias groups\\n   414→        logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: resolved to {len(alias_groups)} characters\\\")\\n   415→        for canonical, aliases in sorted(alias_groups.items(), key=lambda x: -len(x[1])):\\n   416→            if aliases:\\n   417→                logger.info(f\\\"  '{canonical}' <- aliases: {aliases}\\\")\\n   418→            else:\\n   419→                logger.debug(f\\\"  '{canonical}' (no aliases)\\\")\\n   420→\\n   421→        # Build final characters\\n   422→        characters = []\\n   423→        low_confidence = []\\n   424→\\n   425→        for canonical_name, aliases in alias_groups.items():\\n   426→            # Collect all mentions for this character\\n   427→            all_mentions = []\\n   428→            all_strategies = set()\\n   429→            all_confidences = []\\n   430→            chapters_present = set()\\n   431→            all_types = []  # Track character types from all proposals\\n   432→\\n   433→            # Get mentions from canonical name\\n   434→            if canonical_name in name_groups:\\n   435→                for result in name_groups[canonical_name]:\\n   436→                    all_mentions.extend(result.proposal.mentions)\\n   437→                    all_strategies.add(result.proposal.strategy)\\n   438→                    all_confidences.append(result.overall_score)\\n   439→                    chapters_present.add(result.proposal.chapter_index)\\n   440→                    # Collect character type if available\\n   441→                    if hasattr(result.proposal, 'character_type'):\\n   442→                        all_types.append(result.proposal.character_type)\\n   443→\\n   444→            # Get mentions from aliases\\n   445→            for alias in aliases:\\n   446→                if alias in name_groups:\\n   447→                    for result in name_groups[alias]:\\n   448→                        all_mentions.extend(result.proposal.mentions)\\n   449→                        all_strategies.add(result.proposal.strategy)\\n   450→                        all_confidences.append(result.overall_score)\\n   451→                        chapters_present.add(result.proposal.chapter_index)\\n   452→                        # Collect character type if available\\n   453→                        if hasattr(result.proposal, 'character_type'):\\n   454→                            all_types.append(result.proposal.character_type)\\n   455→\\n   456→            if not all_mentions:\\n   457→                continue\\n   458→\\n   459→            # Deduplicate mentions by position (same position = same mention)\\n   460→            # This handles cases where NER and LLM both find the same mention\\n   461→            seen_positions = set()\\n   462→            unique_mentions = []\\n   463→            for mention in all_mentions:\\n   464→                if mention.position not in seen_positions:\\n   465→                    seen_positions.add(mention.position)\\n   466→                    unique_mentions.append(mention)\\n   467→            all_mentions = unique_mentions\\n   468→\\n   469→            # Sort mentions by position\\n   470→            all_mentions.sort(key=lambda m: m.position)\\n   471→\\n   472→            # Calculate final confidence\\n   473→            if not all_confidences:\\n   474→                error_msg = f\\\"No confidences available for character '{canonical_name}' - cannot continue\\\"\\n   475→                logger.error(error_msg)\\n   476→                raise ValueError(error_msg)\\n   477→            avg_confidence = sum(all_confidences) / len(all_confidences)\\n   478→\\n   479→            # Boost confidence for multiple strategies or many chapters\\n   480→            if len(all_strategies) > 1:\\n   481→                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.1)\\n   482→            if len(chapters_present) > 3:\\n   483→                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.05)\\n   484→\\n   485→            # Boost confidence based on mention count\\n   486→            # High-mention characters should have high confidence (major characters)\\n   487→            mention_count = len(all_mentions)\\n   488→            if mention_count >= 100:\\n   489→                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.15)\\n   490→            elif mention_count >= 50:\\n   491→                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.10)\\n   492→            elif mention_count >= 20:\\n   493→                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.05)\\n   494→\\n   495→            # Determine final character type by majority vote (prefer non-UNCERTAIN)\\n   496→            final_type = CharacterType.UNCERTAIN\\n   497→            if all_types:\\n   498→                type_counts = {}\\n   499→                for t in all_types:\\n   500→                    if t != CharacterType.UNCERTAIN:\\n   501→                        type_counts[t] = type_counts.get(t, 0) + 1\\n   502→                if type_counts:\\n   503→                    final_type = max(type_counts.keys(), key=lambda t: type_counts[t])\\n   504→\\n   505→            # LLM fallback for uncertain character types\\n   506→            if final_type == CharacterType.UNCERTAIN and self.llm:\\n   507→                final_type = self._llm_classify_character_type(\\n   508→                    canonical_name, all_mentions, chapters_present\\n   509→                )\\n   510→\\n   511→            # Create character\\n   512→            char_id = self._generate_id(canonical_name)\\n   513→            first_chapter = min(chapters_present) if chapters_present else 1\\n   514→\\n   515→            character = Character(\\n   516→                id=char_id,\\n   517→                canonical_name=canonical_name,\\n   518→                aliases=list(aliases),\\n   519→                mentions=all_mentions,\\n   520→                first_appearance_chapter=first_chapter,\\n   521→                mention_count=len(all_mentions),\\n   522→                chapters_present=sorted(chapters_present),\\n   523→                confidence=avg_confidence,\\n   524→                supporting_strategies=list(all_strategies),\\n   525→                character_type=final_type,\\n   526→            )\\n   527→\\n   528→            if avg_confidence >= self.confidence_threshold:\\n   529→                characters.append(character)\\n   530→            else:\\n   531→                low_confidence.append(character)\\n   532→\\n   533→        # Sort by mention count\\n   534→        characters.sort(key=lambda c: c.mention_count, reverse=True)\\n   535→        low_confidence.sort(key=lambda c: c.mention_count, reverse=True)\\n   536→\\n   537→        total_mentions = sum(c.mention_count for c in characters)\\n   538→        total_mentions += sum(c.mention_count for c in low_confidence)\\n   539→\\n   540→        return CharacterMap(\\n   541→            characters=characters,\\n   542→            low_confidence_characters=low_confidence,\\n   543→            total_mentions=total_mentions,\\n   544→            total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n   545→            pipeline_metadata={\\n   546→                \\\"high_confidence_count\\\": len(characters),\\n   547→                \\\"low_confidence_count\\\": len(low_confidence),\\n   548→                \\\"confidence_threshold\\\": self.confidence_threshold,\\n   549→                \\\"used_llm_aliases\\\": self.use_llm_alias_resolution,\\n   550→            },\\n   551→        )\\n   552→\\n   553→    def _group_by_name(\\n   554→        self,\\n   555→        results: list[CharacterValidationResult],\\n   556→    ) -> dict[str, list[CharacterValidationResult]]:\\n   557→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Group validation results by character name.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   558→        groups = defaultdict(list)\\n   559→        for result in results:\\n   560→            groups[result.proposal.name].append(result)\\n   561→        return dict(groups)\\n   562→\\n   563→    def _heuristic_alias_resolution(\\n   564→        self,\\n   565→        name_groups: dict[str, list[CharacterValidationResult]],\\n   566→        all_results: list[CharacterValidationResult],\\n   567→    ) -> dict[str, list[str]]:\\n   568→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   569→        Resolve aliases using heuristics.\\n   570→\\n   571→        Returns dict mapping canonical name to list of aliases.\\n   572→        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   573→        # Start with each name as its own group\\n   574→        alias_map = {name: set() for name in name_groups.keys()}\\n   575→\\n   576→        # Collect alias candidates from validation\\n   577→        alias_candidates = defaultdict(set)\\n   578→        for result in all_results:\\n   579→            name = result.proposal.name\\n   580→            for candidate in result.alias_candidates:\\n   581→                alias_candidates[name].add(candidate)\\n   582→\\n   583→        names = list(name_groups.keys())\\n   584→\\n   585→        # Find matches based on name components\\n   586→        for i, name1 in enumerate(names):\\n   587→            for name2 in names[i + 1:]:\\n   588→                if self._names_match(name1, name2):\\n   589→                    # Merge: keep longer/more complete name as canonical\\n   590→                    # Calculate mention counts for both names\\n   591→                    count1 = sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in name_groups[name1])\\n   592→                    count2 = sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in name_groups[name2])\\n   593→                    canonical, alias = self._pick_canonical(name1, name2, count1, count2)\\n   594→                    if canonical in alias_map:\\n   595→                        alias_map[canonical].add(alias)\\n   596→                        # Merge alias's aliases\\n   597→                        if alias in alias_map:\\n   598→                            alias_map[canonical].update(alias_map[alias])\\n   599→                            del alias_map[alias]\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650\",\"uuid\":\"53a80284-7595-455d-8f46-3be8e815a7c9\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py\",\"content\":\"        Args:\\n            llm_client: LLM for alias resolution\\n            confidence_threshold: Threshold for high-confidence characters\\n            use_llm_alias_resolution: Whether to use LLM for alias resolution\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.llm = llm_client\\n        self.confidence_threshold = confidence_threshold\\n        self.use_llm_alias_resolution = use_llm_alias_resolution and llm_client is not None\\n\\n    def build_consensus(\\n        self,\\n        validations: list[CharacterValidationResult],\\n        total_chapters: int,\\n    ) -> CharacterMap:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Build the final character map from validated proposals.\\n\\n        Args:\\n            validations: All validation results from all chapters\\n            total_chapters: Total number of chapters in document\\n\\n        Returns:\\n            Final CharacterMap with merged characters\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: received {len(validations)} validations\\\")\\n\\n        # Filter to valid proposals\\n        valid_results = [v for v in validations if v.is_valid]\\n        invalid_count = len(validations) - len(valid_results)\\n        if invalid_count > 0:\\n            logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: filtered {invalid_count} invalid proposals\\\")\\n\\n        if not valid_results:\\n            return CharacterMap(\\n                characters=[],\\n                low_confidence_characters=[],\\n                total_mentions=0,\\n                total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n                pipeline_metadata={\\\"warning\\\": \\\"No valid character proposals found\\\"},\\n            )\\n\\n        # Group by name (exact match first)\\n        name_groups = self._group_by_name(valid_results)\\n        logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: grouped into {len(name_groups)} unique names\\\")\\n\\n        # Log the top names by mention count\\n        sorted_names = sorted(\\n            name_groups.items(),\\n            key=lambda x: sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in x[1]),\\n            reverse=True\\n        )\\n        for name, results in sorted_names[:20]:\\n            mentions = sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in results)\\n            chapters = sorted(set(r.proposal.chapter_index for r in results))\\n            logger.debug(f\\\"  '{name}': {mentions} mentions, chapters {chapters}\\\")\\n        if len(sorted_names) > 20:\\n            logger.debug(f\\\"  ... and {len(sorted_names) - 20} more names\\\")\\n\\n        # Separate proper names from descriptive handles\\n        proper_name_groups = {}\\n        epithet_groups = {}\\n        for name, results in name_groups.items():\\n            if self._is_descriptive_handle(name):\\n                epithet_groups[name] = results\\n                logger.debug(f\\\"Classified as epithet: '{name}'\\\")\\n            else:\\n                proper_name_groups[name] = results\\n                logger.debug(f\\\"Classified as proper name: '{name}'\\\")\\n\\n        if epithet_groups:\\n            logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: found {len(epithet_groups)} descriptive handles\\\")\\n            logger.info(f\\\"Epithets: {list(epithet_groups.keys())}\\\")\\n        if proper_name_groups:\\n            logger.info(f\\\"Proper names: {list(proper_name_groups.keys())}\\\")\\n\\n        # Resolve aliases for proper names\\n        if self.use_llm_alias_resolution and len(proper_name_groups) > 1:\\n            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: using LLM alias resolution\\\")\\n            alias_groups = self._llm_alias_resolution(proper_name_groups)\\n        else:\\n            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: using heuristic alias resolution\\\")\\n            alias_groups = self._heuristic_alias_resolution(proper_name_groups, valid_results)\\n\\n        # Resolve aliases for epithets separately\\n        if epithet_groups and self.use_llm_alias_resolution:\\n            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: running epithet alias resolution\\\")\\n            epithet_alias_groups = self._llm_epithet_resolution(epithet_groups)\\n            # Merge epithet alias groups into main alias groups\\n            for canonical, aliases in epithet_alias_groups.items():\\n                alias_groups[canonical] = aliases\\n        elif epithet_groups:\\n            # No LLM - just add epithets as separate characters\\n            for name in epithet_groups:\\n                alias_groups[name] = []\\n\\n        # Cross-group resolution: link epithets to proper names (e.g., \\\"the prince\\\" -> \\\"Prince Prospero\\\")\\n        if epithet_groups and proper_name_groups and self.use_llm_alias_resolution:\\n            logger.info(\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: running cross-group (epithet-to-proper) resolution\\\")\\n            cross_merges = self._llm_cross_group_resolution(epithet_groups, proper_name_groups)\\n            # Apply cross-group merges\\n            for epithet_name, proper_name in cross_merges.items():\\n                if proper_name in alias_groups and epithet_name in alias_groups:\\n                    # Add epithet as alias to proper name\\n                    alias_groups[proper_name].append(epithet_name)\\n                    # Also add any aliases the epithet had\\n                    alias_groups[proper_name].extend(alias_groups[epithet_name])\\n                    # Remove epithet as standalone character\\n                    del alias_groups[epithet_name]\\n                    logger.info(f\\\"Cross-group merge: '{proper_name}' <- epithet '{epithet_name}'\\\")\\n\\n        # Merge name_groups to include epithets for downstream processing\\n        name_groups.update(epithet_groups)\\n\\n        # Log alias groups\\n        logger.info(f\\\"CharacterConsensusBuilder: resolved to {len(alias_groups)} characters\\\")\\n        for canonical, aliases in sorted(alias_groups.items(), key=lambda x: -len(x[1])):\\n            if aliases:\\n                logger.info(f\\\"  '{canonical}' <- aliases: {aliases}\\\")\\n            else:\\n                logger.debug(f\\\"  '{canonical}' (no aliases)\\\")\\n\\n        # Build final characters\\n        characters = []\\n        low_confidence = []\\n\\n        for canonical_name, aliases in alias_groups.items():\\n            # Collect all mentions for this character\\n            all_mentions = []\\n            all_strategies = set()\\n            all_confidences = []\\n            chapters_present = set()\\n            all_types = []  # Track character types from all proposals\\n\\n            # Get mentions from canonical name\\n            if canonical_name in name_groups:\\n                for result in name_groups[canonical_name]:\\n                    all_mentions.extend(result.proposal.mentions)\\n                    all_strategies.add(result.proposal.strategy)\\n                    all_confidences.append(result.overall_score)\\n                    chapters_present.add(result.proposal.chapter_index)\\n                    # Collect character type if available\\n                    if hasattr(result.proposal, 'character_type'):\\n                        all_types.append(result.proposal.character_type)\\n\\n            # Get mentions from aliases\\n            for alias in aliases:\\n                if alias in name_groups:\\n                    for result in name_groups[alias]:\\n                        all_mentions.extend(result.proposal.mentions)\\n                        all_strategies.add(result.proposal.strategy)\\n                        all_confidences.append(result.overall_score)\\n                        chapters_present.add(result.proposal.chapter_index)\\n                        # Collect character type if available\\n                        if hasattr(result.proposal, 'character_type'):\\n                            all_types.append(result.proposal.character_type)\\n\\n            if not all_mentions:\\n                continue\\n\\n            # Deduplicate mentions by position (same position = same mention)\\n            # This handles cases where NER and LLM both find the same mention\\n            seen_positions = set()\\n            unique_mentions = []\\n            for mention in all_mentions:\\n                if mention.position not in seen_positions:\\n                    seen_positions.add(mention.position)\\n                    unique_mentions.append(mention)\\n            all_mentions = unique_mentions\\n\\n            # Sort mentions by position\\n            all_mentions.sort(key=lambda m: m.position)\\n\\n            # Calculate final confidence\\n            if not all_confidences:\\n                error_msg = f\\\"No confidences available for character '{canonical_name}' - cannot continue\\\"\\n                logger.error(error_msg)\\n                raise ValueError(error_msg)\\n            avg_confidence = sum(all_confidences) / len(all_confidences)\\n\\n            # Boost confidence for multiple strategies or many chapters\\n            if len(all_strategies) > 1:\\n                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.1)\\n            if len(chapters_present) > 3:\\n                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.05)\\n\\n            # Boost confidence based on mention count\\n            # High-mention characters should have high confidence (major characters)\\n            mention_count = len(all_mentions)\\n            if mention_count >= 100:\\n                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.15)\\n            elif mention_count >= 50:\\n                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.10)\\n            elif mention_count >= 20:\\n                avg_confidence = min(1.0, avg_confidence + 0.05)\\n\\n            # Determine final character type by majority vote (prefer non-UNCERTAIN)\\n            final_type = CharacterType.UNCERTAIN\\n            if all_types:\\n                type_counts = {}\\n                for t in all_types:\\n                    if t != CharacterType.UNCERTAIN:\\n                        type_counts[t] = type_counts.get(t, 0) + 1\\n                if type_counts:\\n                    final_type = max(type_counts.keys(), key=lambda t: type_counts[t])\\n\\n            # LLM fallback for uncertain character types\\n            if final_type == CharacterType.UNCERTAIN and self.llm:\\n                final_type = self._llm_classify_character_type(\\n                    canonical_name, all_mentions, chapters_present\\n                )\\n\\n            # Create character\\n            char_id = self._generate_id(canonical_name)\\n            first_chapter = min(chapters_present) if chapters_present else 1\\n\\n            character = Character(\\n                id=char_id,\\n                canonical_name=canonical_name,\\n                aliases=list(aliases),\\n                mentions=all_mentions,\\n                first_appearance_chapter=first_chapter,\\n                mention_count=len(all_mentions),\\n                chapters_present=sorted(chapters_present),\\n                confidence=avg_confidence,\\n                supporting_strategies=list(all_strategies),\\n                character_type=final_type,\\n            )\\n\\n            if avg_confidence >= self.confidence_threshold:\\n                characters.append(character)\\n            else:\\n                low_confidence.append(character)\\n\\n        # Sort by mention count\\n        characters.sort(key=lambda c: c.mention_count, reverse=True)\\n        low_confidence.sort(key=lambda c: c.mention_count, reverse=True)\\n\\n        total_mentions = sum(c.mention_count for c in characters)\\n        total_mentions += sum(c.mention_count for c in low_confidence)\\n\\n        return CharacterMap(\\n            characters=characters,\\n            low_confidence_characters=low_confidence,\\n            total_mentions=total_mentions,\\n            total_chapters=total_chapters,\\n            pipeline_metadata={\\n                \\\"high_confidence_count\\\": len(characters),\\n                \\\"low_confidence_count\\\": len(low_confidence),\\n                \\\"confidence_threshold\\\": self.confidence_threshold,\\n                \\\"used_llm_aliases\\\": self.use_llm_alias_resolution,\\n            },\\n        )\\n\\n    def _group_by_name(\\n        self,\\n        results: list[CharacterValidationResult],\\n    ) -> dict[str, list[CharacterValidationResult]]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Group validation results by character name.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        groups = defaultdict(list)\\n        for result in results:\\n            groups[result.proposal.name].append(result)\\n        return dict(groups)\\n\\n    def _heuristic_alias_resolution(\\n        self,\\n        name_groups: dict[str, list[CharacterValidationResult]],\\n        all_results: list[CharacterValidationResult],\\n    ) -> dict[str, list[str]]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Resolve aliases using heuristics.\\n\\n        Returns dict mapping canonical name to list of aliases.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # Start with each name as its own group\\n        alias_map = {name: set() for name in name_groups.keys()}\\n\\n        # Collect alias candidates from validation\\n        alias_candidates = defaultdict(set)\\n        for result in all_results:\\n            name = result.proposal.name\\n            for candidate in result.alias_candidates:\\n                alias_candidates[name].add(candidate)\\n\\n        names = list(name_groups.keys())\\n\\n        # Find matches based on name components\\n        for i, name1 in enumerate(names):\\n            for name2 in names[i + 1:]:\\n                if self._names_match(name1, name2):\\n                    # Merge: keep longer/more complete name as canonical\\n                    # Calculate mention counts for both names\\n                    count1 = sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in name_groups[name1])\\n                    count2 = sum(r.proposal.mention_count for r in name_groups[name2])\\n                    canonical, alias = self._pick_canonical(name1, name2, count1, count2)\\n                    if canonical in alias_map:\\n                        alias_map[canonical].add(alias)\\n                        # Merge alias's aliases\\n                        if alias in alias_map:\\n                            alias_map[canonical].update(alias_map[alias])\\n                            del alias_map[alias]\",\"numLines\":300,\"startLine\":300,\"totalLines\":2317}}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_014ynAmQnxymMGWc7hWpvVQy\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\