{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01D2f3YSuejBbJaREavu7rFY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see! In the output, the character list has \"the Prince Prospero\" with the article, but the chapter summary has \"Prince Prospero\" WITHOUT the article. \n\nNow the crucial question: Is \"Prospero\" (without \"the\") also being extracted as a separate name, and then being merged with \"the Prince Prospero\"? Let me check the aliases again:\n\n```json\n\"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n\"aliases\": [\n  \"Prospero\",\n  \"the mummer\"\n],\n```\n\nAH-HA! \"Prospero\" is an alias. So we have:\n- \"the Prince Prospero\" (proper name with article)\n- \"Prospero\" (proper name without article)  \n- \"the mummer\" (epithet)\n\nThe system correctly merged \"Prospero\" with \"the Prince Prospero\". But it ALSO merged \"the mummer\" with them.\n\nNow let me think about the classification:\n- \"the Prince Prospero\" → 2 capitalized words → PROPER NAME\n- \"Prospero\" → no \"the\" prefix → PROPER NAME\n- \"the mummer\" → 1 word after \"the\" → EPITHET\n\nSo \"the mummer\" should go through cross-group resolution. But wait... what if \"the mummer\" is ALSO being extracted as just \"mummer\" (without \"the\"), and THAT variant is being classified as a proper name and getting merged during proper name alias resolution?\n\nLet me check if we can see this in the raw text:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":981,"cache_read_input_tokens":73515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":981,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650","uuid":"2bed6290-2bbb-4010-8443-03dc01cfeb8b"}
