{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_0171NBTyb2wtGnm7dVJ9jLYC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**BINGO! The death scene is 221 characters, but the context window is only 200 characters!**\n\nThis means:\n- When \"Prince Prospero\" is mentioned, the context captures 200 chars around it\n- When \"the mummer\" is mentioned, the context captures 200 chars around it  \n- But they are 221 chars apart, so NEITHER context contains BOTH names!\n\nThe death detection at line 2036 fails because:\n```python\nif has_death and has_epithet and has_proper:\n    return True  # Block merge\n```\n\nThis requires BOTH names in the SAME context, but with a 200-char window, we can't capture both!\n\n## ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED\n\n**Issue:** False character merge: \"the mummer\" merged with Prince Prospero\n\n**Root Cause:** `src/agents/config.py:line 72` - `character_mention_context_chars = 200` is TOO SMALL to capture the death scene where both characters appear (221 chars).\n\n**Why 11 attempts failed:**\n- Attempts 1-6: Modified cross-group resolution logic (death detection code)\n- Attempts 7-11: Increased context window, but not enough (100 → 150 → 400 for LLM prompt context, but mention extraction context only went to 200)\n\n**The fix:** Increase `character_mention_context_chars` from 200 to at least 250 characters to capture the full death scene."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":78648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1013,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fe6b989-b18f-4021-8711-3f849a1bf650","uuid":"59a48f6f-c091-4c16-9ff3-3465f41bc76c"}
